\h Yehoshua
\toc1 Yehoshua
\toc2 Yehoshua
\toc3 Yehoshua
\mt1 Yehoshua
\mt2 (Joshua)
\is1 Introduction
\ip This account about Yehoshua, traditionally ‘Joshua’ in English (after ‘I’ and then ‘J’ changed over the centuries from a ‘Y’ sound), tells how the Israelis invaded Canaan and took control of the land. Yehoshua led them forward now after replacing Mosheh (Moses) when he passed away somewhere on a mountain. Some of the main events described in this document include: their crossing the Yordan river, the demolition of Yeriho (traditionally ‘Jericho’), the war at Ay, the allocation of blocks of land to the various Israeli tribes and others, and the renewal of the agreement between God and his people.
\ip The most well-known saying in this account is, “…choose for yourselves today who you will serve… But as for me and my household, we will serve Yahweh.” (24:15).
\iot Main components of this account
\io1 The defeat of the Canaanites \ior 1:1–12:24\ior*
\io1 The division of land \ior 13:1–21:45\ior*
\io2 a. The land east of the River Yordan \ior 13:1-33\ior*
\io2 b. The land west of the River Yordan \ior 14:1–19:51\ior*
\io2 c. The refuge cities \ior 20:1-9\ior*
\io2 d. The cities for Levites \ior 21:1-45\ior*
\io1 The returning home of some tribes back to the east of the Yordan \ior 22:1-34\ior*
\io1 Yehoshua's final instructions \ior 23:1-16\ior*
\io1 The renewal of the agreement there at Shikim \ior 24:1-33\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
\c 1
\s1 Yahweh encourages Yehoshua
\rem /s1 God Commands Joshua to Conquer Canaan; God's Commission to Joshua; The Lord Commands Joshua; The Lord's Charge to Joshua; Prelude to the conquest of Canaan
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 After¦99058 the death¦99059 of Yahweh's¦99062 servant Mosheh \add !(Moses¦99060)\add*, Yahweh spoke to¦99065 Mosheh's¦99072 servant Yehoshua \add !(Joshua)\add* (the son¦99068 of Nun¦99070), saying¦99063,
\v 2 “Now that my servant¦99076 Mosheh¦99075 is dead, you¦99085 and all \add #these\add* people¦99088 \add ≈should pack up\add* \add and\add* cross¦99080 over this \add River\add* Yordan¦99083 \add to go\add* to the land¦99092 that I am¦99095 about¦99095 to give¦99095 to them—to Yisra'el's¦99098 descendants.
\v 3 I'll give¦99110 you¦99109 all every place¦99102 that¦99103 the¦99105 \add #soles\add* of your¦99107 \add #feet\add* tread¦99104 on¦99108, just¦99111 like I told Mosheh¦99115.\x + \xo 1:3-5: \xt Deu 11:24-25.\x*
\v 4 Your \add ≈territory¦99137 will extend\add* from the wilderness¦99117 \add in the south\add* to the Lebanon¦99118 \add mountains in the north\add*, and from the large¦99123 Euphrates¦99126 River \add in the east\add*, and \add ≈right to the Mediterranean\add* sea¦99132 \add ≈in the west\add*, including¦99118 all of¦99134 the Hittites' land¦99128.
\v 5 No man will¦99141 \add ≈be able to¦99143 challenge your leadership as long as you live\add*—I'll¦99152 be with you just as I was with Mosheh¦99151—I won't¦99154 fail you or abandon¦99157 you.\x + \xo 1:5: \xt Deu 31:6,8; Heb 13:5.\x*
\v 6 Be¦99160 strong¦99159 and¦99160 be¦99160 courageous¦99160, for you yourself will¦99163 \add ≈lead\add* \add #these\add* people¦99166 to inherit¦99163 the land¦99170 that I promised their¦99174 ancestors¦99174 that I'd give¦99175 to them.\x + \xo 1:6: \xt Deu 31:6-7,23.\x*
\v 7 Just be strong¦99179 and¦99180 very courageous¦99180—making sure that you \add ≈obey everything\add* that my servant¦99190 Mosheh¦99189 instructed¦99188 you. Don't¦99191 turn¦99193 away to the right¦99195 or to the left¦99196 from¦99194 it¦99194, so¦99197 that you'll be wise in every¦99199 \add ≈situation that you end up in\add*.
\v 8 That¦99225 book¦99206 of¦99206 the law¦99207 \add ^must always be on your lips\add* and you should meditate¦99210 on it day¦99212 and night¦99213, so¦99214 that you'll be careful to¦99217 follow everything¦99217 that's written¦99219 in¦99220 it, because¦99221 then you'll make¦99224 your ways¦99227 prosperous and then you'll be wise.
\v 9 Didn't I order you to be strong¦99233 and¦99234 courageous¦99234? Don't¦99231 tremble or be discouraged¦99240 because¦99241 your¦99244 god¦99244 Yahweh¦99243 will be with¦99245 you wherever¦99246 you go¦99247.”
\s1 Yehoshua instructs the people
\rem /s1 Preparations for the Invasion; Joshua Gives Orders to the People; Joshua's Charge to the Israelites
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 10 Then Yehoshua instructed¦99250 the leaders of¦99254 the people¦99255,
\v 11 “Go right through the camp¦99261 and tell the people¦99265: Get everything ready that you'll all need because¦99270 in¦99260 three¦99273 days¦99274 we'll be ready to cross¦99276 over¦99276 this¦99280 river and enter the land¦99285 that your god¦99288 Yahweh¦99287 is¦99289 about¦99289 to give¦99289 to you, and to take¦99282 control of¦99291 it¦99291.”
\p
\v 12 To¦99294 the descendants of Reuben and Gad, and to¦99296 the half-tribe of Menashsheh¦99298, Yehoshua said¦99299,\x + \xo 1:12-15: \xt Num 32:28-32; Deu 3:18-20; Josh 22:1-6.\x*
\v 13 “Remember¦99303 what Yahweh's¦99313 servant¦99311 Mosheh¦99310 informed you: Your god¦99316 Yahweh is¦99317 about give this land¦99323 to you and¦99319 to \add ≈enable you all to settle down\add*.
\v 14 Your women and children and your livestock¦99328 will¦99329 stay \add here\add* in¦99335 the land that¦99331 Mosheh¦99334 \add ≈allocated\add* to¦99333 you on¦99335 \add ≈this eastern\add* side¦99335 of the Yordan¦99336 River. But¦99328 your \add soldiers\add* must¦99329 dress for battle¦99339 and cross¦99338 over¦99338 ahead of your brothers¦99341 and help¦99345 them¦99346
\v 15 until Yahweh enables your brothers¦99354 to \add ≈take over the land that¦99363 your god¦99366 Yahweh is¦99367 about¦99367 to give¦99367 them so they can settle like you all have\add*. Then you'll all be able to return¦99369 to this land which Yahweh's¦99352 servant¦99379 Mosheh¦99378 gave¦99376 you on¦99381 \add ≈this eastern side¦99381 of the Yordan¦99382 and take full control of it¦99373\add*.”
\p
\v 16 “We'll¦99389 do¦99395 everything¦99398 you've¦99394 told¦99394 us to¦99396,” the people answered¦99386, “and¦99396 we'll go¦99402 wherever¦99400 you send¦99401 us.
\v 17 We'll listen¦99412 to you just like we listened¦99407 to everything¦99404 Mosheh said. May¦99415 your¦99417 god¦99417 Yahweh¦99416 be¦99415 with you, just like he¦99420 was¦99420 with Mosheh.
\v 18 We'll put¦99444 anyone to death¦99444 who¦99428 rebels¦99430 against¦99430 your words¦99439 or refuses to follow your instructions. Just stay strong¦99446 and¦99447 courageous¦99447.”
\c 2
\s1 Spies sent to Yeriho/Jericho
\rem /s1 In central Canaan; Rahab Protects the Spies; Rahab and the Spies; Spies Sent to Jericho; Joshua Sends Spies into Jericho
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then from \add there at\add* \add ≈Acacia Grove\add*, Yehoshua (Nun's¦99455 son¦99453) secretly¦99463 sent¦99450 off two¦99459 spies¦99462, saying¦99464, “Go¦99465 \add ≈and learn about the land¦99469 over there, especially around\add* Yeriho¦99472 \add !(Jericho¦99472) City¦99472\add*.” \add ≈So¦99472\add* they went¦99473 off, and \add over there,\add* they entered the house¦99475 of a woman¦99477—a prostitute¦99478 named Rahab¦99480—and they lay¦99481 down¦99481 there.\x + \xo 2:1: \xt Heb 11:31; Jam 2:25.\x*
\v 2 \add ≈However, someone told¦99485\add* Yeriho's¦99487 king¦99486, “Listen, some Israeli¦99495 men¦99490 arrived here tonight to \add ≈check out¦99496 our\add* land¦99499.”
\v 3 So¦99501 the king¦99502 sent¦99501 \add guards\add* to tell Rahab¦99506, “Bring¦99503 out the men¦99509 who \add ≈went¦99510 to your¦99515 place\add* and¦99501 \add ≈stayed the night\add*, because¦99516 they've come¦99523 here to \add ≈check out\add* our land¦99522!”
\p
\v 4 \add ≈However, Rahab had hidden¦99531\add* the two¦99529 men \add ≈so she¦99531 answered\add*, “Indeed, the men \add ≈arrived here, but¦99525\add* I didn't¦99538 know¦99539 where¦99540 they were from.
\v 5 \add ≈But¦99543 as\add* the \add city\add* gate¦99544 was¦99545 \add ≈about¦99545\add* to shut¦99545 \add ≈last night\add*, the men¦99547 went out¦99548. I¦99550 don't¦99549 know¦99550 to where¦99551 \add *they¦99552\add* went—if you all hurry, you might be able to \add ≈catch\add* them.”
\v 6 (\add ≈But¦99560 actually\add* she had¦99561 taken¦99561 them up¦99561 onto her \add flat\add* roof¦99562 and¦99560 hidden¦99563 them in¦99564 \add ≈bundles of¦99564 flax that¦99566 were drying there\add*.)
\v 7 \add ≈So¦99576\add* the \add ≈guards hurried\add* out on the road¦99575 to the fords¦99578 on the Yordan¦99576 \add River\add* and¦99579 the \add city\add* gate¦99579 was kept shut after \add *they\add* had¦99583 left.
\p
\v 8 Before the Israeli men lay¦99589 down¦99589 \add to sleep that night\add*, \add @Rahab\add* went¦99591 up them¦99592 on¦99593 the roof¦99595
\v 9 and told \add *them\add*, “\add #We\add* know¦99601 that Yahweh¦99605 has¦99604 given¦99604 this land to you all and we're \add ≈all terrified\add* of you. Everyone¦99601 that lives here is \add ≈trembling at the thought of your¦99613 coming\add*
\v 10 because¦99623 we've heard that¦99639 Yahweh¦99629 dried¦99628 up¦99628 the water¦99632 of the Red Sea¦99633 ahead of you all when¦99637 you left¦99637 Egypt¦99638 \add !(Mitsrayim¦99638)\add*. And¦99638 \add ≡we heard\add* what you all did¦99640 to¦99641 two¦99641 of the Amorite¦99643 kings¦99642 Sihon¦99647 and Og¦99648 over the Yordan¦99646 there—how you all completely destroyed¦99650 them.\x + \xo 2:10: a \xt Exo 14:21; \xo b \xt Num 21:21-35.\x*
\v 11 \add ≈Yes,\add* we've heard¦99653 \add <the reports\add* and \add ≈we trembled and lost our¦99655 courage to fight you¦99662 all\add* because¦99662 your¦99665 god¦99665 Yahweh¦99664, he's¦99666 God¦99665 \add ≈over\add* the heavens¦99668 above¦99669 and the earth¦99672 below¦99673.
\v 12 \add ≈So¦99675\add* now¦99675, please¦99678 promise me by¦99680 Yahweh¦99680 that because¦99681 I've¦99683 been kind to \add both of\add* you, you all will¦99695 act kindly towards my father's¦99693 household¦99692. Give¦99695 me \add ≈a guarantee that you'll do¦99686 what you promise\add*
\v 13 and spare¦99700 my parents and my siblings and their families from¦99723 death¦99723.”
\p
\v 14 “Our lives \add ≈for your lives\add*,” the \add two\add* men¦99727 agreed. “If¦99731 you don't¦99732 tell¦99733 \add ≈anyone about our¦99736 agreement\add*, then¦99725 when Yahweh¦99741 gives¦99739 us this land¦99745, we'll \add ≈show\add* kindness and¦99725 faithfulness¦99749 to you.”
\p
\v 15 Then¦99751 she put a rope¦99752 out through¦99753 the window¦99754 to let¦99751 them¦99751 down¦99751 \add to escape from the city\add*, because¦99755 her¦99756 house¦99756 where she lived was¦99757 \add actually built into\add* the side of¦99757 the wall.
\v 16 “Go to the hill¦99765 country¦99765,” she told them, “\add ≈so those searching for you won't find\add* you, and¦99763 hide¦99772 \add up\add* there¦99773 for three¦99774 days¦99775. \add Then once\add* the searchers have returned, you'll be able to \add safely\add* \add ≈return¦99777 to your camp\add*.”
\p
\v 17 “\add ≈This¦99789 promise that¦99790 you made¦99791 us¦99791 make\add*,” the men¦99785 told her, “\add ≈won't apply unless you do this\add*:
\v 18 \add Take\add* this red cord¦99799 \add and\add* when we¦99794 \add ≈invade\add* the land, tie \add *it\add* in this window¦99804 \add ≈in the wall\add*. Make sure that¦99805 your parents and your siblings and their households¦99820 are all here in your house¦99824.
\v 19 If any of them leaves the house, \add ≈their life will¦99836 then¦99826 be in their own¦99836 hands\add* and¦99826 we'll be innocent \add if they're killed\add*. But¦99826 if anyone with¦99836 you¦99842 in this house \add ≈gets injured\add*, \add ≈we'll be responsible for that\add*.
\v 20 \add ≈Also¦99856,\add* if¦99853 you tell¦99855 anyone else about this agreement, then¦99853 we'll be¦99860 \add ≈released\add* from¦99862 this promise that¦99863 you made¦99864 us¦99864 make.”
\v 21 “\add ≈Sure¦99874, let it¦99866 be¦99868 as you say¦99866\add*,” \add @Rahab\add* \add ≈responded¦99866\add*. Then¦99866 she sent¦99871 them¦99871 off¦99871, and¦99866 after they'd gone¦99872, she tied¦99873 the red cord¦99876 in¦99878 her window¦99878.
\p
\v 22 \add @The two men\add* went¦99881 up into the hills and stayed there¦99884 for three¦99885 days¦99886 until¦99887 the search party returned¦99889 \add to the city\add* after searching all¦99893 the roads and not¦99896 finding¦99897 them¦99897.
\v 23 \add ≈So¦99899\add* the two¦99900 men¦99901 went¦99902 down¦99902 to the river and crossed¦99904 over¦99904 and returned¦99899 to Yehoshua¦99908 (Nun's¦99911 son¦99909), and they¦99905 told him¦99914 everything that¦99918 had¦99918 happened¦99918.
\v 24 “Yahweh¦99928 has¦99927 certainly given¦99927 this land to us,” they told Yehoshua. “The people there won't be able to resist us because¦99942 they're so terrified.”
\c 3
\s1 The Israelis cross the Yordan
\rem /s1 Israel Crosses the Jordan; The Israelites Cross the Jordan; The People of Israel Cross the Jordan; Crossing the Jordan
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Early¦99945 the next morning¦99947, Yehoshua \add and the people\add* got up early¦99945 and set¦99948 off from Acacia Grove and went¦99950 as far as the Yordan¦99953 \add River\add* and camped¦99959 there¦99960 without crossing over¦99962.
\v 2 After three¦99966 days¦99967, the leaders went¦99968 throughout the camp¦99971
\v 3 and instructed¦99973 the people¦99976, “As soon as you all see the box¦99980 \add containing\add* the agreement¦99981 with your god¦99984 Yahweh¦99983, and \add ≡see\add* the Levitical¦99986 priests¦99985 carrying¦99987 it, then¦99973 you yourselves should move out¦99990 from¦99991 your places¦99991 and follow after¦99993 it.
\v 4 But¦100000 keep about¦100002 nine hundred metres back from it. Don't¦100005 go any closer than that so that you all can see the¦100015 way to go, because¦100020 \add ≈we haven't been this way\add* before.”
\p
\v 5 Then Yehoshua told the people¦100032, “\add ≈Make sure you¦100038 all do the ritual washing to make yourselves¦100033 pure\add*, because¦100034 tomorrow¦100035 Yahweh¦100037 will¦100036 do miracles among us.”
\v 6 And¦100042 \add *he¦100041\add* told the priests¦100045, “Lift¦100047 up the box¦100050 with the agreement¦100051, and \add ≈walk across here in front\add* of the people.” \add ≈So¦100041\add* they¦100055 lifted¦100055 up the \add sacred\add* chest¦100050 and went¦100060 \add ≈and stood in front of all\add* the people.
\p
\v 7 Then Yahweh¦100066 told Yehoshua, “Today I'll¦100072 begin¦100072 to make¦100073 you powerful in¦100074 the eyes¦100074 of¦100074 all¦100075 Yisrael¦100077 \add !(Israel¦100077)\add* so they'll know¦100079 that¦100071 I'm with you just¦100081 like I was¦100082 with Mosheh¦100085.
\v 8 Tell the priests¦100093 who¦100094 are carrying¦100094 the \add sacred\add* chest¦100095 that as soon as they come¦100099 to¦100100 the edge¦100102 of the river, they should \add ≈go in¦100105 just a little and¦100089 then¦100089 stop there\add*.”
\p
\v 9 Then Yehoshua told the Israelis¦100114, “\add ≈Gather around\add* here and listen¦100117 to your¦100122 god¦100122 Yahweh's¦100121 message¦100120.”
\v 10 \add *He¦100124\add* told \add <them\add*, “This¦100126 is how you'll all know¦100127 that¦100126 God¦100129, who can do anything, is among you. With your¦100131 own eyes, you'll all see how he'll take away the land from¦100134 the Canaanites¦100137, the Hittites¦100140, the Hivites¦100143, the Perizzites¦100146, the Girgashites¦100149, the Amorites¦100150, and¦100124 the Yebusites.
\v 11 Listen, the sacred chest¦100154 containing the slabs that belongs to the master¦100156 who \add owns\add* the whole¦100157 world, is¦100160 about¦100160 to \add be taken\add* across the Yordan¦100162 in¦100162 front of you¦100161.
\v 12 \add ≈So¦100171\add* now¦100164, \add ≈select one man¦100169 from¦100170 each of¦100170 your twelve tribes¦100170\add*,
\v 13 and¦100180 as soon as the \add ≈priests¦100184 carrying¦100185 the sacred chest¦100186 go into the Yordan¦100193, as soon as their feet¦100183 touch the water, the river water on¦100192 the upstream side\add* will¦100198 pile up in¦100192 a heap¦100201.”
\p
\v 14 \add ≈So¦100204 once the people¦100206 had packed up their¦100207 tents¦100207 ready to¦100208 cross¦100208 the river\add*, the priests¦100212 carrying¦100213 the sacred box¦100214 walked ahead in¦100205 front¦100216 of them.
\v 15 Then¦100219 as soon as \add ≈those¦100220 priests¦100226\add* steeped into the \add edge\add* of the \add ≈fast-flowing\add* river (because it¦100233 overflowed its¦100238 banks¦100238 at¦100230 harvest¦100241 time¦100240 \add in the spring\add*),
\v 16 then¦100243 the water coming¦100245 from upstream \add suddenly\add* stopped flowing. The water far upstream piled up near a town¦100255 called Adam¦100253 (near Tsaretan), and¦100243 the water that¦100256 normally flowed down¦100259 towards the Sea of¦100261 Aravah¦100262 (\add also called\add* the Dead Sea or the Salt¦100265 Sea) \add ≈stopped flowing\add*, so the people¦100268 were able to cross \add what was\add* the Yordan River opposite Yeriho¦100271 \add !(Jericho¦100271)\add*.
\v 17 The priests¦100274 carrying¦100275 the sacred chest¦100276 with¦100280 Yahweh's¦100279 agreement¦100277 \add in it\add*, stood¦100273 on firm, dry ground in \add what had been\add* the middle¦100281 of¦100282 the river. All¦100284 the Israelis crossed¦100296 over¦100287 on dry ground until¦100289 everyone was across.
\c 4
\s1 The memorial of boulders
\rem /s1 Twelve Stones Set Up at Gilgal; Memorial Stones Are Set Up; Memorials to the Jordan Crossing
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Once all¦100305 the people had¦100304 crossed¦100308 over¦100308 the Yordan¦100311 River, Yahweh¦100314 told Yehoshua,
\v 2 “Take \add those\add* twelve men¦100327 \add ≈that the¦100324 people¦100324 selected from¦100334 each tribe¦100334\add*,
\v 3 and give them these instructions: Pick up¦100339 twelve boulders¦100352 from here¦100342 in the middle¦100343 of¦100343 the Yordan¦100344 from near where the priests¦100347 are standing¦100345, and bring them over with¦100358 you, and put them in the place¦100358 where you all camp tonight.”
\p
\v 4 \add ≈So\add* Yehoshua called¦100366 \add over\add* the twelve men, one from¦100383 each tribe¦100383,
\v 5 and told them¦100386, “Cross¦100387 \add ≈back to where\add* your god¦100392 Yahweh's¦100391 box¦100390 is in¦100389 the middle¦100395 of the Yordan¦100396 and \add ≈each of you¦100398 should pick up a rock¦100400 and carry it back on your\add* shoulder—one stone¦100400 each on your shoulder to match the number¦100405 of tribes¦100406 of Yisra'el's¦100409 sons.
\v 6 \add ≈Those boulders will¦100423 be¦100412 a monument for all the people\add*. \add ≈In the future when your¦100419 children¦100419 ask¦100418 what those boulders mean\add*,
\v 7 then¦100427 you'll all be able to¦100428 tell them¦100428 that the water in the Yordan¦100432 River was cut¦100440 off¦100440 ahead of the box¦100434 with¦100438 Yahweh's¦100437 agreement¦100435. When¦100427 it¦100438 crossed¦100438 over into the river, the water in the river \add ≈stopped flowing\add*, and¦100443 those boulders¦100444 are a memorial¦100446 for¦100447 the Israelis¦100448 forever¦100451.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈So¦100453\add* the Israelis¦100458 did just what Yehoshua had told¦100461 them to do, and they¦100463 picked up¦100463 twelve boulders¦100467 from¦100468 the Yordan¦100469, just as¦100470 Yahweh¦100472 had instructed¦100461 Yehoshua, and brought them over¦100481 to where \add the people\add* were camping and placed¦100485 them down¦100486 there¦100487.
\v 9 Then¦100489 Yehoshua¦100493 stacked up¦100492 twelve other boulders¦100491 in the middle¦100494 of the Yordan¦100495 where the feet¦100498 of the priests¦100499 carrying¦100500 the box¦100501 with the agreement¦100502 had been, and¦100503 they¦100503 remain there¦100504 until¦100505 today.
\v 10 The¦100509 priests¦100509 carrying¦100510 the box¦100511 had stood¦100512 in¦100513 the middle¦100513 of the Yordan¦100514 until¦100515 everything¦100517 that¦100520 Yahweh¦100523 had instructed Yehoshua to pass¦100541 on to the people was done, just as Mosheh¦100535 had \add also\add* instructed Yehoshua, and¦100509 the people had rapidly crossed¦100541 over¦100541.
\p
\v 11 As soon as all¦100547 the people had¦100546 crossed over, the priests¦100555 carrying Yahweh's¦100554 box¦100552 \add also\add* crossed over in¦100556 front¦100556 of¦100556 the people.
\v 12 The¦100572 \add soldiers\add* from the tribes¦100567 of Reuben¦100562, and Gad¦100565 and the half-tribe of Menashsheh¦100568 had \add ≈marched\add* over ahead of the rest of the Israeli¦100571, as¦100573 Mosheh¦100576 had \add ≈agreed with them¦100575\add*.
\v 13 (\add There were\add* around forty¦100578 thousand¦100579 of them, armed and ready for battle, and they¦100582 were heading to the plains¦100587 of Yeriho¦100588 \add !(Jericho¦100588)\add* for the battle \add there\add*.)
\v 14 On that day¦100591, Yahweh¦100594 helped Yehoshua to look powerful in the eyes¦100598 of the people, and¦100602 they respected him¦100603 just¦100604 as¦100604 they had¦100605 respected Mosheh all the days¦100611 of his\f + \fr 4:14 \ft The Hebrew doesn't make it clear here whether the writer meant all of \+bd Mosheh's life\+bd* or all of \+bd Yehoshua's life\+bd*, so translations will vary.\f* life.
\p
\v 15 Then Yahweh¦100616 told Yehoshua,
\v 16 “\add ≈Now order\add* the priests¦100625 carrying¦100626 the box¦100627 with the agreement to come¦100629 up¦100629 out of \add what was\add* the Yordan¦100632 \add River\add*,”
\v 17 so Yehoshua¦100635 instructed¦100634 the priests¦100638 to¦100639 come¦100640 on up¦100640 from¦100641 the Yordan¦100643.
\v 18 As soon as the priests¦100648 carrying¦100649 the box¦100650 with¦100646 Yahweh's¦100653 agreement¦100651 came¦100646 up out¦100656 of¦100659 \add what had been\add* the Yordan¦100655 \add River\add* and their¦100666 feet¦100658 stepped onto \add what had been\add* dry¦100661 land, the river water¦100663 returned¦100662 to¦100666 its¦100675 place¦100666 and overflowed it banks¦100675 as \add ≈it had been doing for the previous few days¦100670\add*.
\p
\v 19 The¦100677 people¦100677 had come up¦100678 from¦100679 the river valley \add ≈around the end of March¦100681\add* and¦100685 they¦100678 camped¦100685 east¦100688 of Yeriho¦100689 \add !(Jericho¦100689)\add* at¦100682 Gilgal¦100686,
\v 20 which¦100696 was where \add #they¦100697\add* had¦100697 set¦100701 up the \add monument of\add* twelve boulders¦100694.
\v 21 Then¦100705 \add @Yehoshua\add* told the Israelis¦100709, “\add ≈In¦100715 the future\add* when your¦100713 descendants ask¦100712 why these¦100721 boulders¦100720 are here,
\v 22 tell them that¦100734 this is where Yisrael¦100730 crossed the Yordan¦100733 \add River\add* on¦100728 dry land.
\v 23 Your¦100745 god¦100740 Yahweh¦100739 dried up the river water¦100743 ahead of you until you'd all crossed over, just¦100749 as¦100749 \add *he\add* had done¦100750 when he dried up the Red Sea before¦100759 we¦100762 crossed over.
\v 24 Yahweh¦100773 did that so that all the peoples¦100768 in the world would know¦100765 that he is¦100775 powerful, \add and\add* so that you'll always all respect him.
\c 5
\rem /s1 The New Generation Circumcised; Circumcision at Gilgal
\p
\v 1 When all the Amorite¦100793 kings who¦100794 were¦100795 on¦100795 the \add west\add* side¦100795 of¦100795 the Yordan (towards the ocean) and all the Canaanite¦100801 kings (beside the ocean) heard¦100789 how¦100807 Yahweh¦100810 had dried¦100809 up¦100809 the water¦100813 in¦100795 the Yordan \add River\add* until¦100819 \add @the Israelis¦100818\add* had crossed¦100821 over¦100821, they¦100821 \add ≈trembled with¦100795 fear\add* and \add ≈lost their¦100824 nerve to stand against\add* Yisrael¦100818.
\s1 Circumcising the males and celebrating ‘pass-over’ at Gilgal
\rem /s1 The Circumcision at Gilgal; Israel Reestablishes Covenant Ceremonies
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 2 At¦100837 that¦100838 time¦100837, Yahweh¦100840 told Yehoshua¦100843, “Make¦100844 yourself¦100845 flint¦100847 knives¦100846 and¦100848 again¦100848 circumcise¦100849 the¦100852 male Israelis¦100854.”
\v 3 So¦100857 Yehoshua¦100860 \add had\add* flint¦100862 knives¦100861 made¦100857 and¦100863 the¦100866 \add male\add* Israelis¦100867 were circumcised¦100863 at \add a place they named\add* ‘The¦100870 hill¦100870 of¦100870 foreskins¦100871’.
\v 4 (This¦100873 was done because all the men¦100887 who'd left¦100882 Egypt¦100883 and¦100873 who were old enough to join the army \add had been circumcised but\add* had died¦100889 in¦100890 the wilderness¦100890 since then¦100873,\x + \xo 5:6: \xt Num 14:28-35.\x*
\v 5 \add and\add* because¦100895 all¦100903 the \add ≈boys\add* who'd been born¦100906 while they were in¦100907 the wilderness¦100907 after they'd left¦100902 Egypt¦100910 hadn't been circumcised¦100897.
\v 6 The¦100920 Israelis¦100922 had spent forty¦100917 years \add ≈moving\add* around the wilderness¦100923 until¦100924 the last of¦100930 those men¦100930 who'd left¦100932 Egypt¦100933 but¦100958 hadn't listened¦100937 to Yahweh \add ≈had died\add*. Yahweh had promised not to let¦100945 them see¦100945 the land that¦100949 \add *he'd¦100951\add* promised to their¦100952 ancestors¦100952 to give¦100953 them—a land flowing¦100956 with¦100923 milk¦100957 and¦100958 honey¦100958.
\v 7 It was the sons of those people¦100975 that Yehoshua had¦100975 circumcised \add this time\add* because¦100968 they¦100971 hadn't been circumcised on¦100977 the way¦100977.)
\p
\v 8 After all¦100983 their¦100988 males had¦100982 been circumcised¦100986, they remained in¦100989 that camp¦100989 until¦100990 they'd \add ≈healed¦100991 up\add*.
\v 9 Then Yahweh¦100995 told Yehoshua, “Today I've¦101000 rolled¦101000 away¦101000 the¦101003 disgrace of¦101003 Egypt¦101004 from¦101005 you,” and¦101006 that¦101013 place¦101008 is named Gilgal\f + \fr 5:9 \ft The name ‘Gilgal’ (‘גִּלְגָּל’, ‘circle’) sounds like ‘galal’ (‘גַּלַל’, ‘roll’).\f* until¦101011 this day.
\rem /s1 The Passover at Gilgal
\p
\v 10 In¦101018 the evening¦101028 of \add ≈the fourth day¦101026 that the people¦101016 had been camped¦101015\add* at¦101019 Gilgal¦101019 there on¦101019 the plains¦101029 near Yeriho¦101030 \add !(Jericho¦101030)\add*, they¦101020 celebrated the ‘pass-over’.\x + \xo 5:10: \xt Exo 12:1-13.\x*
\s1 Eating from the land—no more manna
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 11 The next¦101035 day they ate roasted¦101038 grain¦101038 that \add they'd taken from that area\add*, and¦101032 ate flat bread¦101037 that same day.
\v 12 The¦101054 day¦101045 after¦101045 they'd eaten some¦101047 of the produce from that area, there was no manna¦101055 \add on the ground to be collected\add* and¦101043 \add so\add* it stopped—instead they'd eat the produce from the Canaan¦101059 region¦101058 \add beginning\add* that year¦101060.\x + \xo 5:12: \xt Exo 16:35.\x*
\s1 Yehoshua and the man with a sword
\rem /s1 The Lord's Commander Confronts Joshua; Joshua and the Man with a Sword; The Fall of Jericho; Joshua's Vision
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 13 While Yehoshua was in the Yeriho¦101067 \add !(Jericho¦101067) area\add*, he¦101068 looked up¦101068 and saw¦101070 a man in front¦101075 of him. The man had drawn¦101077 his sword¦101076 and was holding it in his hand¦101078 \add ≈so\add* Yehoshua approached him and asked, “Are¦101085 you¦101085 on¦101065 \em our\em* side, or¦101086 with¦101065 our enemies?”
\p
\v 14 “No¦101092,” the man \add ≈answered\add*, “but¦101090 I, the leader of¦101097 Yahweh's¦101099 army¦101097, have¦101101 come¦101101 now¦101100.”
\p Then¦101090 Yehoshua fell¦101102 \add ≈to his knees\add* and bowed¦101108 down¦101108 with his face¦101106 to the¦101095 ground, and \add ≈asked\add* him¦101110, “What's¦101111 my¦101112 master¦101112 going to \add ≈command¦101095\add* to his servant¦101116?”
\p
\v 15 “Take¦101126 off your sandals¦101128,” the commander¦101119 of Yahweh's¦101122 army¦101121 told \add *him\add*, “because¦101131 the ground that¦101133 you're¦101134 standing¦101135 is¦101137 holy¦101137.” \add ≈So¦101118\add* Yehoshua \add ≈took¦101126 them off\add*.
\c 6
\s1 Yeriho's walls collapse
\rem /s1 Jericho Taken and Destroyed; The Fall of Jericho
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now¦101143\add* Yeriho¦101143 \add !(Jericho¦101143) city\add* was shut-up tightly \add ≈because of¦101146 the¦101147 Israelis¦101148\add*, \add so\add* no one was coming¦101152 out¦101150 and¦101143 no one could go¦101150 in.
\v 2 Then Yahweh¦101156 told Yehoshua, “Listen, I've¦101161 given¦101161 you \add ≈victory over\add* Yeriho¦101165 and its¦101168 king¦101168, and \add ≈their\add* mighty¦101169 army \add >warriors\add*.
\v 3 All¦101176 your soldiers must¦101172 go¦101172 around¦101172 the city¦101182 once every day for six¦101187 days¦101188
\v 4 with¦101198 seven priests \add ≈blowing\add* ram's horns going ahead of the sacred box¦101197. On¦101201 the seventh¦101199 day¦101198, you all must¦101192 go¦101200 around the city¦101203 seven times¦101205 while the priests are blowing the horns.
\v 5 \add ≈Finally¦101217,\add* with¦101211 a long blast¦101211 of¦101213 the horn¦101214, when you all hear¦101215 that then¦101210 all the people¦101224 must¦101221 shout¦101225 loudly¦101226 and the wall¦101228 around¦101230 the city¦101229 will fall¦101227 down flat, and all the \add ≈soldiers\add* should go¦101231 straight¦101234 in¦101211 \add from where they're standing\add*.”
\p
\v 6 \add ≈So¦101236\add* Yehoshua summoned the priests and told them¦101245, “Carry the box with the agreement¦101250, and have seven priests hold up seven rams' horns¦101256 \add ≈ahead\add* of Yahweh's¦101259 box.”
\v 7 Then¦101261 he told the people¦101265, “Go¦101268 across in front¦101273 and¦101261 go¦101267 around¦101267 the city¦101270, \add ≈with the soldiers going ahead\add* of Yahweh's¦101275 box¦101274.”
\p
\v 8 After Yehoshua had¦101278 spoken¦101278 to¦101280 the people¦101282, the seven priests¦101284 with their seven rams' horns went¦101297 across in¦101293 front¦101289 and blew the horns, and the box¦101294 with Yahweh's¦101290 covenant¦101295 was¦101297 \add ≈carried¦101285\add* along behind¦101298 them¦101298.
\v 9 The \add ≈soldiers\add* walked ahead of the priests¦101303 blowing the horns, with¦101313 the rear guard¦101307 walking behind¦101309 the box¦101310. \add So\add* they were walking and¦101300 blowing the horns,
\v 10 and¦101315 Yehoshua told¦101318 the people¦101317, “Don't¦101321 shout \add ≈or even speak or make¦101325 a noise\add* until¦101334 the day¦101335 I tell you all to¦101337 shout—then¦101315 you all should shout loudly.”
\p
\v 11 \add ≈So¦101341\add* Yahweh's¦101344 box¦101342 was carried once around¦101341 the city¦101347, then¦101341 the people went¦101341 back to the camp and¦101341 stayed¦101353 the night¦101353 there.
\p
\v 12 Yehoshua¦101358 got up early¦101357 the next morning¦101359, and the priests¦101361 picked up Yahweh's¦101365 box¦101364
\v 13 and the seven priests¦101368 holding the seven rams' horns went in front of \add *it\add*—blowing¦101378 the horns as they¦101378 kept walking. The¦101387 \add ≈soldiers\add* walking in front of them¦101382, and the rear guard¦101383 walked behind¦101385 Yahweh's¦101375 box¦101374 \add ≈while\add* the horns were being blown.
\v 14 They¦101394 went¦101393 once around¦101393 the city¦101396 on that second¦101398 day¦101397 and¦101401 then¦101393 returned¦101401 to their camp¦101402 \add again\add*—doing¦101404 that for six¦101405 days¦101406.
\p
\v 15 Then¦101408 on the seventh day they got up¦101413 early¦101412 at dawn¦101414 and¦101408 went around the city¦101418 \add ≈as before\add*, except this¦101420 day they went around seven¦101430 times¦101431.
\v 16 \add ≈After that seventh¦101435 time¦101434 around,\add* the priests¦101437 blew \add a long blast\add* on¦101434 the rams' horns and¦101439 Yehoshua told the people¦101443, “Shout¦101444, because¦101445 Yahweh¦101448 has¦101447 given¦101447 you¦101449 all the city¦101452!
\v 17 \add However,\add* everything in the city¦101455 is¦101462 sacred to Yahweh¦101463. Only¦101464 the prostitute¦101466 Rahab¦101465 and¦101454 those who¦101471 are in her¦101472 house¦101473 will be allowed to live¦101467, because¦101474 she¦101475 hid¦101475 the spies that we¦101480 sent¦101480 in.
\v 18 But¦101482 for all of you, everything inside the city is forbidden—if any¦101493 of you take¦101492 anything out of the city then our camp¦101499 \add ≈would also then be marked for destruction¦101491\add* and¦101482 it¦101503 would cause \add a lot of\add* trouble¦101502.
\v 19 All¦101514 the silver¦101507 and gold¦101508, bronze¦101510 and iron¦101511 is¦101512 dedicated to¦101514 Yahweh¦101516 and must¦101517 go¦101517 into \add *his\add* treasury¦101515.
\p
\v 20 \add ≈So¦101519\add* the people shouted¦101532 when that horn blew—as soon as they heard¦101524 \add *it¦101523\add* the people shouted loudly¦101533 and the wall¦101535 fell¦101534 down on¦101522 itself and the people went up \add and over\add* into the city from wherever they were standing and captured¦101542 the city.\x + \xo 6:20: \xt Heb 11:30.\x*
\v 21 They¦101548 \add ≈killed\add* every \add living thing\add* in¦101553 the city¦101553 with¦101553 their \add #swords¦101568\add*, including¦101555 men and women, young¦101558 and old¦101561, even cattle, sheep¦101564, and donkeys¦101565.
\p
\v 22 Then¦101570 Yehoshua¦101577 commanded the two¦101570 men¦101571 who had¦101572 spied¦101572 on the area, “Go¦101578 to the prostitute's¦101582 house¦101579 and bring¦101583 the woman out of it and all who are related to her, just¦101595 as¦101595 you promised her.”
\v 23 \add ≈So¦101599\add* the young¦101600 men¦101600 \add ≈who'd gone in as\add* spies¦101601 went¦101599 in and brought¦101602 out¦101602 Rahab¦101605 and her parents and all¦101623 her relatives and settled them¦101627 outside¦101628 of the camp¦101629 of the Israelis¦101630.
\v 24 Then¦101632 \add @the warriors\add* set fire¦101634 to the city¦101632 and burnt¦101633 everything that¦101637 was¦101639 in¦101634 it¦101639. Only¦101640 the silver¦101642 and gold¦101643, and bronze¦101645 and iron¦101646 were \add first removed and\add* put¦101647 into the treasury¦101648 of Yahweh's¦101651 house¦101649.
\v 25 \add ≈But¦101653\add* Yehoshua spared the prostitute¦101656 Rahab¦101655 and her father's¦101660 household¦101659 and her other relatives because¦101676 she hid¦101677 the men that¦101675 Yehoshua had¦101683 sent¦101683 in to spy¦101685 on¦101671 Yeriho¦101688 \add !(Jericho¦101688)\add*, and she still lives¦101668 in Yisrael¦101672 to this day¦101674.\x + \xo 6:25: \xt Heb 11:31.\x*
\p
\v 26 At¦101693 that¦101694 time¦101693, Yehoshua made \add @the¦101705 people\add* take an¦101691 oath¦101691, saying¦101695,\x + \xo 6:26: \xt 1Ki 16:34.\x*
\q1 “May Yahweh¦101699 curse¦101696 anyone who¦101700 rebuilds¦101702 this city¦101705, Yeriho¦101709 \add !(Jericho¦101709)\add*.
\q1 When that person lays its foundation¦101711, may his oldest son¦101712 die.
\q1 And¦101702 when he¦101702 finishes building¦101702 the city wall and¦101712 sets¦101713 up its gates¦101714, may his youngest¦101712 son die.”
\p
\v 27 \add ≈So¦101716\add* Yahweh¦101717 was¦101716 with¦101718 Yehoshua¦101720 and¦101716 \add ≈everyone in¦101723 that region had heard about him¦101722\add*.
\c 7
\s1 Achan's sin
\rem /s1 Ai Defeats the Israelites; The Sin of Achan and Its Punishment; Achan's Sin
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 \add ≈However\add* the Israelis disobeyed the command about \add ≈not taking anything\add*. Achan¦101734 (son of Karmi, son of Zabdi¦101740, son of Zerah¦101743, from the tribe¦101744 of Yehudah¦101745) took¦101733 something that was prohibited, \add ≈so\add* Yahweh¦101752 was angry with¦101732 the Israelis.
\p
\v 2 \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* Yehoshua sent¦101756 some of his men from Yeriho¦101759 \add !(Jericho¦101759)\add* to Ay (east¦101766 of Beyt-El and near Beyt-Aven) and told them¦101771, “Go¦101773 \add ≈to Ay\add* and spy¦101774 out the land¦101777.” \add ≈So¦101756\add* the men went¦101778 and checkout out Ay.
\v 3 \add ≈When¦101785\add* they returned¦101785 to Yehoshua, they told him¦101790, “Don't \add ≈send all¦101794 the¦101796 warriors\add*—\add only\add* around two¦101797 to three¦101800 thousand¦101797 men should¦101793 go¦101803 and¦101785 attack¦101804 them¦101804. Don't \add ≈bother everyone¦101796 else\add* because¦101818 \add ≈Ay is small\add*.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦101822\add* around three¦101827 thousand¦101828 \add ≈warriors¦101832\add* went¦101822 to \add attack Ay, but they were defeated\add* and¦101830 had to flee¦101830 \add back\add*.
\v 5 The men¦101837 from Ay chased¦101842 them from the city gate¦101844 downhill to Shevarim and fought them on¦101849 the slopes. About thirty-six¦101839 \add ≈of them\add* were killed¦101835, and the \add ≈Israelis¦101853 became very afraid and lost all their courage\add*.
\p
\v 6 Yehoshua and the¦101865 Israeli¦101872 elders¦101872 tore¦101857 their clothes¦101859 \add in grief\add* and fell¦101860 to their knees in front¦101865 of Yahweh's¦101867 box¦101866 until¦101868 evening¦101870, throwing dust¦101875 onto their heads¦101878 \add in despair\add*.
\v 7 Then¦101880 Yehoshua \add ≈asked\add*, “Yahweh¦101885, my¦101884 master¦101884, why¦101886 did you¦101887 bring \add #these\add* people¦101891 across the Yordan¦101905 and then¦101880 let us be defeated and killed by the Amorites¦101899? If¦101901 only we'd been¦101902 content and stayed on¦101898 the other¦101904 side¦101904 of¦101904 the river.
\v 8 Please, my¦101908 master¦101908, what¦101909 can I say¦101910 now that¦101912 \add *we\add* have had to¦101916 flee \add in shame\add* from our enemies¦101917?
\v 9 \add When\add* the Canaanites¦101920 and the other people living in this land¦101923 hear¦101919 \add <about this\add*, they'll surround¦101924 us and \add ≈kill all of¦101929 us\add*. Then¦101919 what¦101933 would you¦101935 do¦101935 to defend your¦101936 honour?
\p
\v 10 \add ≈But¦101940\add* Yahweh¦101941 told Yehoshua, “Stand¦101945 up¦101945! Why is your¦101953 face¦101953 \add ≈on¦101951 the ground like that¦101948\add*?
\v 11 Yisrael¦101956 has¦101955 sinned¦101955 and disobeyed my¦101961 agreement¦101961\f + \fr 7:11 \ft Probably referring to the ten commands written on the stone slabs.\f* that¦101962 I made with them¦101964. They've also taken¦101966 prohibited things¦101969—stealing¦101971, deceiving¦101973, and put¦101975 it with their¦101976 own possessions.
\v 12 \add That's why\add* \add *they\add* were unable to defeat their¦101984 enemies—they had¦101990 to flee from them because¦101989 they took what was prohibited. I won't¦101978 be¦101994 with¦101995 you all again unless you all destroy¦101991 \add ≈what was taken\add*.
\v 13 \add So\add* get up and tell the people¦102007, ‘Purify yourselves¦102009 for tomorrow¦102010, because¦102011 \add *our\add* God¦102015 Yahweh¦102014 says¦102013 that \add ≈we took something prohibited and we won't¦102020 be¦102021 able¦102021 to better our enemies¦102024 until¦102025 it's removed¦102027 from¦102029 among us\add*.
\v 14 \add ≈Tomorrow morning¦102032\add* you¦102031 all must present yourselves by your tribes¦102033. Then the tribe¦102035 that Yahweh \add ≈singles out\add*, must present yourselves by your clans¦102041, and¦102031 the clan that Yahweh \add ≈singles out\add*, must present yourselves by household. Then the household that Yahweh \add ≈singles out\add*, must present yourselves individually.
\v 15 The¦102057 \add >man\add* who¦102057 is¦102057 caught¦102057 will¦102059 be¦102059 destroyed by¦102057 fire¦102060, along with¦102058 everything that¦102066 belongs to¦102068 him¦102068, because¦102075 he's violated Yahweh's¦102074 agreement¦102073 and¦102056 committed a disgraceful¦102078 sin among Yisrael¦102079.”
\rem /s1 Achan's Sin
\p
\v 16 \add ≈So¦102081\add* Yehoshua got up early¦102081 the next morning¦102083 and \add ≈ordered each tribe to¦102088 come forward singly\add*, and the tribe of¦102090 Yehudah¦102091 was¦102089 \add ≈singled out\add*.
\v 17 Then¦102093 each of the clans came forward and the Zerahite clan was \add ≈singled out\add*, and when their families¦102107 came forwards, Zabdi's¦102109 household was \add ≈singled out\add*.
\v 18 When¦102111 everyone in that \add ≈extended family¦102114\add* came forward¦102111, Achan¦102117 (son of Karmi¦102120, son of Zabdi¦102123, son of Zerah¦102126, from the¦102127 tribe¦102127 of Yehudah¦102128) was \add ≈singled out\add*.
\v 19 Then¦102130 Yehoshua told Achan¦102134, “My son¦102135, now \add ≈honour\add* Yahweh¦102140 the¦102141 god¦102141 of¦102141 Yisrael¦102142 and¦102130 give¦102143 thanks to¦102145 him¦102145. And¦102147 tell¦102147 me now what¦102151 you've done¦102152—don't¦102153 hide¦102155 it from¦102156 me.”
\p
\v 20 “It's true,” Achan¦102159 replied, “I've¦102166 sinned¦102166 against Yahweh¦102167 the¦102168 god¦102168 of¦102168 Yisrael¦102169. This is what I did¦102172:
\v 21 I saw¦102174 a \add ≈beautiful Babylonian cloak¦102177\add* and two¦102181 hundred silver pieces and a tongue-shaped¦102184 piece of¦102189 gold¦102185 (weighing¦102189 six-hundred grams) \add there inside Yeriho/Jericho\add*. I wanted them so I took¦102191 them, and they're hidden¦102193 in¦102176 the ground under my¦102196 tent¦102196, with¦102176 the silver underneath.”
\p
\v 22 Yehoshua¦102201 sent¦102200 some messengers¦102202 and they¦102203 ran¦102203 to¦102204 the tent¦102204, and sure enough, it¦102206 was¦102206 all hidden¦102206 there \add in the ground\add* with¦102207 the silver¦102208 underneath¦102209.
\v 23 They¦102211 took¦102211 it out of the tent¦102213 and brought¦102214 it back to¦102215 Yehoshua and all¦102219 the people¦102221, and spread¦102223 it out in¦102224 front¦102224 of Yahweh¦102225.
\p
\v 24 Then¦102227 Yehoshua took¦102227 Achan¦102231 and the silver¦102237, the cloak¦102240, the gold¦102244 along with his children and his animals, his tent¦102262 and everything he owned, and took them to¦102269 the Akor Valley¦102276 along with all the people,
\v 25 and he¦102279 said¦102279, “Why¦102281 did you cause trouble for us¦102282? Yahweh¦102284 will¦102283 trouble you today.” And \add ≈the people executed him by throwing rocks at him\add*. Then¦102279 they¦102293 threw rocks at them¦102294 \add all\add* and burnt¦102293 \add the bodies\add*
\v 26 and piled rocks¦102304 over them which are still there¦102313 to this day and Yahweh's¦102310 \add ≈anger¦102312 subsided\add*. That's¦102319 why that¦102308 place¦102318 is called¦102316 ‘Akor’ \add (i.e., ‘Trouble’)\add* Valley¦102320 to this day.
\c 8
\s1 The defeat and destruction of Ay
\rem /s1 Ai Destroyed; The Capture and Destruction of Ai; The Israelites Defeat Ai; Ai Captured by a Stratagem and Destroyed
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦102328 told Yehoshua, “Don't¦102332 \add ≈be afraid or discouraged¦102337\add*. Take¦102338 all your¦102351 warriors with¦102351 you and go¦102346 to Ay. Listen, I've¦102350 given¦102350 \add ≈you victory over\add* Ay's king¦102354 and his people and his city¦102361 and his land¦102364.
\v 2 You'll do¦102366 to Ay and its king what you did to Yeriho \add !(Jericho)\add* and its king,\f + \fr 8:2 \ft We're not actually given any details about what happened to the king of Yeriho.\f* except that you all can plunder its spoil and its livestock for yourselves¦102381. Ambush the city from¦102384 behind.”
\p
\v 3 \add ≈So¦102386\add* Yehoshua \add ≈led\add* his warriors towards Ay. \add *He¦102386\add* chose¦102394 thirty¦102396 thousand¦102397 of¦102390 the \add ≈bravest and strongest warriors\add* and sent¦102401 them¦102401 \add ≈ahead in the darkness\add*
\v 4 and told¦102404 them¦102405, “Listen¦102405, you all lie¦102409 in¦102409 ambush against¦102410 the¦102412 city¦102412 from¦102416 close behind¦102411 \add *it¦102404\add*, and \add ≈make sure you all stay alert and ready\add* \add to attack\add*.
\v 5 \add ≈I will bring those warriors\add* who are with¦102440 me and¦102424 we'll approach the¦102433 city¦102433, then¦102424 when they¦102437 come¦102437 out¦102437 to¦102438 \add ≈attack\add* us¦102438 like \add ≈last time\add*, we'll run back away from them¦102442.
\v 6 They'll¦102448 \add ≈think we're running away from them like we did before, so they'll chase after¦102445 us until¦102446 we've drawn¦102447 them away\add* from the city¦102451.
\v 7 Then¦102461 you'll all \add ≈move in¦102471\add* from¦102463 your ambush¦102463 \add position\add* and capture the city, and your god¦102470 Yahweh¦102469 \add ≈will give¦102468 the city to you all\add*.
\v 8 \add ≈After\add* you capture¦102474 the city, set¦102478 fire to¦102483 it¦102473. Do¦102485 what I've¦102487 ordered¦102487 you all \add ≈which in¦102482 turn has come from\add* Yahweh¦102484.
\v 9 \add ≈So¦102490\add* Yehoshua sent¦102490 them¦102490 to¦102493 \add set up\add* the ambush¦102495 between¦102497 Ay and¦102490 Beyt-El (so west¦102503 of¦102504 Ay). \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* \add *he\add* stayed overnight \add ≈at¦102507 the camp\add*.
\p
\v 10 Yehoshua got up early¦102512 in the morning¦102514 and gathered the \add ≈warriors\add*, then¦102512 he and the Israeli¦102521 elders¦102521 went \add ≈in front¦102523 of them\add* \add to go and attack\add* Ay.
\v 11 \add *They all\add* went¦102533 close to the city¦102537 and camped¦102538 \add there slightly\add* to the north¦102539, with just a valley between¦102544 them and Ay¦102540.
\v 12 (He¦102548 had sent around five¦102549 thousand¦102550 warriors to \add ≈lie in\add* ambush¦102554 between¦102555 Beyt-El and¦102548 Ay, west¦102561 of¦102549 the city¦102562,
\v 13 \add ≈so\add* the main group was¦102572 to the north¦102572 and¦102564 the rear guard¦102576 to the west¦102577.) That¦102582 night¦102581 Yehoshua¦102580 went¦102579 down into the valley¦102584.
\v 14 When¦102586 the king of¦102588 Ay saw¦102587 \add <the Israelis¦102604\add*, he hurriedly¦102591 got his men¦102594 ready, and went out¦102593 early¦102592 to meet¦102597 Yisrael¦102599 for the battle¦102600. The king and his people¦102604 went to a \add ≈prepared spot overlooking the Yordan valley, but¦102586\add* he didn't¦102609 know¦102610 that¦102611 \add ≈another group lay in ambush¦102613 behind¦102615 the city¦102616\add*.
\v 15 Yehoshua and¦102618 the Israeli group allowed themselves to be struck¦102618 by them¦102623, then¦102618 they¦102624 fled¦102624 back towards the wilderness¦102626
\v 16 and all¦102629 the \add ≈men\add* in¦102633 the city were called¦102628 out to¦102635 chase them¦102636. \add ≈So¦102628\add* they¦102637 chased after¦102638 Yehoshua¦102639 and were drawn¦102640 away from¦102641 the city,
