\p
\v 1 \add ≈There were several kings¦103090 who ruled in regions on¦103092 this west side¦103092 of the Yordan¦103093—the Hittites¦103104 and Amorites¦103105, the Canaanites¦103106 and Perizzites¦103107, the Hivites¦103108 and the Yebusites. Some were in the hill country¦103094, some in the lowlands¦103095, and some along the Mediterranean coast¦103097 south of Lebanon¦103103\add*. \add When\add* \add *they\add* heard¦103087 about \add @what had happened at¦103092 Ay\add*,
\v 2 they¦103111 \add ≈formed an alliance\add* to fight¦103113 \add together\add* against Yehoshua¦103116 and¦103117 Yisrael¦103119.
\p
\v 3 \add ≈However,\add* when \add the people who\add* live in Gibeon¦103125 heard¦103126 what Yehoshua had¦103129 done¦103129 to¦103131 Yeriho¦103131 \add !(Jericho¦103131)\add* and¦103132 Ay,
\v 4 they¦103134 \add ≈decided to use cunning¦103138\add* \add instead\add*. They¦103137 \add ≈found old, worn-out sacks¦103142 to throw over their¦103144 donkeys¦103144 and old, worn-out wineskins that had been torn and mended¦103149, then¦103134 sent men to act¦103140 as¦103140 ambassadors¦103140\add*.
\v 5 \add ≈They found worn-out sandals¦103151 that had been patched¦103153, and wore worn-out clothes¦103155.\add* All¦103158 the \add ≈food¦103159 that they took for the journey was already dry and disintegrating into crumbs¦103163\add*.
\v 6 They¦103165 went¦103165 to Yehoshua in the camp¦103171 at Gilgal¦103172 and told him¦103174, “We've come¦103181 from¦103179 a far-off land¦103179 and \add ≈want you to make¦103183 a treaty with\add* us¦103185.”
