\v 8 They¦103207 \add ≈addressed\add* Yehoshua, “We¦103212 are¦103217 your¦103211 servants¦103211.”
\p Yehoshua \add ≈asked\add* them¦103214, “Who¦103216 are you? And¦103218 where¦103218 have you come¦103219 from¦103218?”
\p
\v 9 “Your¦103227 servants¦103227 have¦103226 come¦103226 from¦103223 a very¦103225 distant¦103224 land¦103223,” they¦103226 replied, “because¦103228 of the reputation¦103228 of your¦103230 god¦103230, Yahweh¦103229. We've heard¦103233 the \add #reports¦103234\add* about him¦103234 and¦103221 everything that¦103238 he¦103239 did¦103239 in¦103240 Egypt¦103240,
\v 10 and everything that¦103246 he¦103247 did¦103247 to¦103248 the two¦103248 Amorite¦103250 kings¦103249 on¦103252 the other¦103252 side¦103252 of the Yordan¦103253—King Sihon¦103254 of Heshbon¦103256, and King Og¦103257 of the Bashan¦103260 who¦103261 \add ≈lived\add* in¦103252 Ashtaroth¦103262.\x + \xo 9:10: \xt Num 21:21-35.\x*
\v 11 \add ≈So¦103264\add* our elders¦103266 and all¦103267 those who live in¦103273 our area instructed us, ‘Take¦103272 provisions¦103274 for the \add ≈journey¦103275\add* and go¦103276 to¦103277 meet¦103277 them, and tell them, “We are your¦103273 servants¦103280. \add ≈Now¦103282 make¦103283 a treaty with¦103273\add* us.” ’
