\rem /s1 The Amorites Are Defeated; The Sun Stands Still; The conquest of the south; Israel Defeats the Southern Kings
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Once\add* King¦103585 Adoni¦103582-Tsedek¦103584 of Yerushalem¦103586 heard that Yehoshua had captured¦103589 Ay and completely destroyed¦103594 it¦103580, and that he'd treated the king of Ay the same as¦103595 he had treated the king of Yeriho¦103597 \add !(Jericho¦103597)\add*, and he heard that the Gibeonites had made peace with¦103612 Yisrael¦103610 and were¦103611 \add now working for\add* them,
\v 2 \add @the people of Yerushalem\add* were very afraid¦103614 because¦103623 Gibeon¦103619 had been a powerful city¦103617, stronger than¦103626 Ay, and¦103614 all¦103629 it's¦103624 warriors¦103632 were powerful.
\v 3 \add ≈So¦103634\add* King Adoni¦103635-Tsedek¦103637 sent¦103634 to¦103640 King Hoham¦103642 of Hebron¦103645, King Piram¦103648 of Yarmut, King Yafia¦103654 of Lakish, and¦103634 King Debir¦103660 of Eglon¦103663, saying¦103664,
\v 4 “Come \add ≈here\add* and help¦103669 me¦103669. We'll attack¦103670 Gibeon¦103673 because¦103674 they've made¦103676 peace¦103676 with¦103677 Yehoshua and \add ≈the¦103682 Israelis¦103683\add*.”
\v 5 \add ≈So¦103685\add* those five¦103687 Amorite¦103690 kings¦103689 (from Yerushalem¦103692, Hebron¦103695, Yarmut, Lakish, and Eglon¦103704) joined together to go¦103686 to Gibeon¦103712 and their¦103708 \add armies\add* camped¦103709 there to fight against¦103714 it¦103714.
