\v 28 Then Yehoshua captured¦104202 Makkedah that¦104205 \add same\add* day¦104204. \add #They\add* killed \add ≈the king and everyone¦104217 else in¦104222 the city\add*, leaving¦104224 no survivors¦104225, and \add @Yehoshua\add* did the same to the king of Makkedah as¦104229 he'd done¦104230 to the king of Yeriho \add !(Jericho)\add*.\f + \fr 10:28 \ft We're not actually given any details about what happened to the king of Yeriho/Jericho.\f*
\rem /s1 Southern Cities Conquered
\p
\v 29 Then¦104234 Yehoshua and all¦104236 Yisrael¦104238 went \add southwest\add* from¦104240 Makkedah¦104240 to Libnah¦104241 and fought¦104242 against \add *it\add*.
\v 30 Yahweh¦104248 also¦104249 \add ≈allowed Yisrael¦104253 to conquer\add* it¦104251 and its king, and \add @Yehoshua\add* \add again\add* \add ≈killed everyone¦104264 in¦104252 the city\add*, leaving¦104272 no survivors¦104274, and he did the same to the king of Libnah as¦104277 he'd done¦104278 to the king of Yeriho¦104280 \add !(Jericho¦104280)\add*.
\p
\v 31 Then Yehoshua and all¦104285 Yisrael¦104287 went \add south\add* from¦104289 Libnah¦104289 to¦104290 Lakish, \add ≈where\add* they took a position against \add @the city\add* and fought¦104293 against it¦104294.
\v 32 On the second¦104305 day¦104304 \add of the battle\add*, Yahweh¦104297 \add ≈helped Yisrael¦104302 defeat Lakish\add*, and \add #they\add* captured¦104303 it¦104306 and \add ≈killed everyone¦104312 in¦104301 the city\add* like \add #they\add* had¦104321 done¦104321 to Libnah¦104322.
\v 33 King¦104328 Horam¦104327 of¦104328 Gezer¦104329 arrived to¦104330 help¦104330 Lakish, \add ≈but¦104334\add* Yehoshua defeated¦104334 him¦104334 and his¦104338 men, leaving¦104342 no survivors¦104345.
\p
\v 34 Then¦104347 Yehoshua and \add ≈the Israelis\add* went \add west\add* from¦104353 Lakish to¦104354 Eglon¦104354, \add ≈where\add* they¦104355 took a position against \add @the city\add* and fought¦104357 against it¦104358.
\v 35 That day \add #they\add* captured¦104360 it and¦104360 \add ≈killed everyone¦104368 in¦104373 the city\add* like \add #they\add* had¦104380 done¦104380 to Lakish.
\p
\v 36 Then Yehoshua and \add ≈the Israelis\add* went \add west\add* from¦104390 Eglon¦104390 up \add into the hills\add* to¦104391 Hebron¦104391, and fought¦104392 against¦104393 it¦104393.
\v 37 They¦104395 captured¦104395 it¦104395 and killed the king¦104403 and everyone in¦104416 all their \add ≈towns\add*, leaving¦104419 no survivors¦104420 the same as Eglon¦104425.
\p
\v 38 Then Yehoshua and \add ≈the Israelis\add* went to¦104444 \add the city of\add* Debir¦104444 and fought¦104445 against¦104446 it¦104446.
\v 39 They captured¦104448 \add @the city\add* and its king and all¦104454 their \add ≈towns\add*, killing everyone¦104464 and leaving¦104471 no survivors¦104472. \add #They\add* treated Debir¦104479 and its king just like they had¦104474 to Libnah¦104483 and Hebron¦104475 and their kings.
\p
\v 40 \add ≈So¦104486\add* Yehoshua \add ≈attacked and conquered the entire¦104490 region\add*—the hill¦104493 country¦104493 and the Negev¦104494, the lowlands¦104495 and the slopes¦104496, and all¦104498 their¦104500 kings¦104500. He didn't¦104501 leave¦104502 any survivors¦104503 \add ≈but¦104486\add* destroyed¦104508 everything¦104505 living, just¦104509 as¦104509 Yisrael's¦104513 god¦104512 Yahweh¦104511 had¦104510 commanded¦104510.
\v 41 Yehoshua \add ≈attacked and conquered\add* them¦104515 from¦104517 Kadesh-Barnea and as far as Gaza¦104521, all¦104523 the¦104525 land¦104525 of¦104525 Goshen¦104526 and as far as Gibeon¦104529.
\v 42 In one swoop, Yehoshua captured¦104539 all those kings¦104534 and¦104531 their¦104538 land¦104538, because¦104543 Yisrael's¦104546 god¦104545 Yahweh¦104544 had fought¦104547 for¦104548 Yisrael.
\v 43 Then¦104550 Yehoshua and¦104552 \add ≈his warriors\add* returned¦104550 to their camp¦104558 at Gilgal¦104559.
\c 11
\s1 Yehoshua defeats the northern kings
\rem /s1 Joshua Defeats Jabin and His Allies; The conquest of the north; Israel Defeats the Northern Kings; The United Kings of Northern Canaan Defeated; Northern Kings Defeated
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now when\add* King Yabin¦104564 of Hatsor heard¦104563 \add <about all that\add*, he¦104568 sent¦104568 to¦104569 King Yovav of Madon¦104573 and the¦104576 kings of Shimron¦104577 and Akshaf,
\v 2 as well as the kings¦104585 from¦104587 the hill country¦104588 in the north¦104587 and in \add ≈the rift valley plains\add* south¦104590 of Lake Galilee, and in the lowlands¦104592 and in the heights¦104593 of Dor¦104594 in the west¦104595,
\v 3 and \add ≡the kings of\add* the Canaanites both east¦104598 and west¦104599, and the Amorites¦104600, Hittites¦104601, Perizzites¦104602, and the Yebusites who lived in the hill country¦104604, and to the Hivites¦104605 by \add Mt.\add* Hermon¦104607 in the Mitspah region¦104608.
\v 4 \add ≈So¦104611\add* they \add all\add* came out with their¦104615 warriors—so many people¦104617 that¦104621 they were as many as the \add grains of\add* sand¦104620 on the seashore, along with many horses¦104628 and¦104611 chariots¦104629.
\v 5 All¦104635 those kings¦104636 gathered¦104634 together¦104640 at the time they'd specified and¦104634 took up positions at the Merom¦104644 stream to fight¦104645 against Yisrael¦104648.
\p
\v 6 \add ≈But¦104651\add* Yahweh¦104652 told Yehoshua, “Don't¦104656 be¦104658 afraid¦104658 that \add ≈they look overwhelming\add*, because¦104660 tomorrow¦104662 at¦104681 this¦104664 time¦104663, I'll¦104665 \add ≈ensure that they're all¦104669 slain¦104670 by\add* Yisrael¦104672. You'll hamstring¦104676 their horses¦104675 and¦104677 burn¦104680 their chariots¦104679.”
\v 7 Then¦104683 Yehoshua¦104684 and all¦104685 \add ≈his warriors\add* went¦104683 to Merom¦104694 and attacked them¦104697 \add ≈without warning\add*
\v 8 and¦104699 Yahweh¦104700 \add ≈enabled them to defeat¦104704 them\add*.
\v 9 Then¦104727 Yehoshua¦104729 did \add ≈what Yahweh¦104734 had¦104731 instructed\add* him—he crippled their horses¦104737 and¦104727 set fire¦104743 to their chariots¦104741.
\p
\v 10 \add ≈After that¦104749,\add* Yehoshua returned to Hatsor \add city\add* and captured¦104750 it and killed the king¦104756—in¦104748 the past it had been the head¦104764 of¦104764 all¦104765 those kingdoms¦104767.
\v 11 They¦104790 killed everything¦104773 in¦104778 \add @the¦104775 city\add*—not leaving¦104784 anything that breathes¦104787—and¦104770 then¦104770 set fire¦104792 to¦104779 it¦104784.
\p
\v 12 \add ≈So¦104794\add* Yehoshua¦104808 \add had\add* captured¦104807 all¦104796 those kings¦104799 and their cities¦104798, and completely destroyed¦104813 \add @them and their people\add* just¦104815 as¦104815 Yahweh's¦104819 servant¦104818 Mosheh¦104817 had commanded¦104816.
\v 13 \add However,\add* other than Hatsor, they didn't¦104829 burn¦104830 any of¦104822 the¦104824 \add other more defensible\add* cities¦104824 built \add up\add* on¦104826 mounds¦104828.
\v 14 The \add ≈Israelis¦104848\add* took any valuables and any livestock¦104844 from those cities¦104842, but¦104840 they killed everyone¦104847 and everything else.
\v 15 Yehoshua did¦104884 everything exactly as Yahweh¦104871 had instructed his¦104875 servant¦104875 Mosheh (and¦104883 as Mosheh had then instructed him), not \add ≈forgetting or ignoring\add* anything¦104889.
\s1 Yehoshua controls the entire region
\rem /s1 Summary of Joshua's Conquests; The Territory Taken by Joshua
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 16 Yehoshua¦104900 conquered the whole¦104903 region—the hill country and all the Negev¦104912, all of the Goshen¦104917 region, the lowlands and \add ≈the rift valley plains\add*, the hill country of Yisrael¦104927 and its¦104928 lowlands
\v 17 from Mt. Halak¦104933 downhill towards Seir¦104935, and as far as Baal¦104938-Gad¦104939 in¦104940 the Lebanon¦104941 valley¦104940 below Mt. Hermon¦104945. He attacked and captured¦104950 all their¦104949 kings¦104949 and executed them.
\v 18 Yehoshua¦104957 had spent \add ≈quite some time\add* battling¦104964 with¦104958 those kings¦104962.
\v 19 No city¦104969 made¦104971 peace¦104971 with¦104984 \add ≈the Israelis¦104975\add* except¦104976 for the Hivites¦104977 who lived in Gibeon¦104979—all the rest were taken¦104983 in battle¦104984
\v 20 because¦105007 it¦104990 was¦104990 Yahweh who'd \add ≈made them stubborn\add* so¦105008 they'd fight against Yisrael¦104999 and be completely destroyed¦105009 without any \add ≈mercy\add*. \add Yes,\add* they were annihilated just¦105010 as¦105010 Yahweh had¦105011 instructed¦105011 Mosheh¦105015.\x + \xo 11:20: \xt Deu 7:16.\x*
\p
\v 21 At¦105020 that¦105021 time¦105020, Yehoshua \add also\add* went¦105018 and exterminated the Anakites¦105025 from the hill country, from Hebron¦105031, Debir¦105034, Anab, and all¦105038 the hill country of¦105039 Yehudah¦105040 and Yisrael¦105043. \add *He¦105044\add* completely destroyed¦105047 them from their¦105046 cities¦105046.
\v 22 No \add ≈descendants of Anak\add* were left¦105052 in Yisrael¦105056, except that \add some\add* remained¦105061 in Gaza¦105058, in Gat¦105059, and¦105060 in Ashdod¦105060.
\p
\v 23 Yehoshua captured the entire¦105067 region, just as Yahweh¦105073 had¦105072 told Mosheh¦105076, and Yehoshua gave¦105077 it¦105077 as an¦105079 inheritance¦105079 to Yisrael¦105080, divided into portions according¦105081 to their tribes¦105082, and then¦105063 the region \add ≈was¦105084 peaceful¦105084\add*.
