\p
\v 1 These¦105113 are¦105090 the kings¦105090 in the region¦105100 who the \add ≈Israelis¦105096 defeated¦105093\add* on¦105101 the eastern side¦105101 of the Yordan¦105102 \add river\add* and took¦105097 possession¦105097 of their¦105100 land from the Arnon¦105106 riverbed¦105105 \add in the south\add* to¦105107 Mt¦105109. Hermon¦105110 \add in the north\add*, including¦105088 all of the eastern \add ≈rift valley plains\add*:\x + \xo 12:1-5: \xt Num 21:21-35; Deu 2:26–3:11.\x*
\v 2 King¦105117 Sihon of the Amorites¦105118 who lived¦105119 in¦105120 Heshbon¦105120 and ruled¦105121 \add over\add* Aroer¦105122 (on¦105120 the edge¦105126 of the Arnon¦105129 riverbed) and \add over\add* half¦105132 of Gilead¦105133 up to the Yabbok¦105135 riverbed \add which formed\add* the border¦105137 with¦105120 the Ammonites¦105139,
\v 3 as well as the \add ≈eastern¦105146 rift valley plains\add* down to Lake Galilee and to the Sea of Aravah¦105149 (\add also called\add* the Dead Sea or the Salt Sea), the road to Beyt-Yeshimot and the area southward¦105157 below the slopes¦105159 of \add Mt.\add* Pisgah¦105160.
\p
\v 4 \add The Israelis also defeated\add* King¦105164 Og¦105163 from Bashan¦105165, \add ≈one of the few remaining\add* Refa'ites, who¦105168 lived¦105168 in¦105169 Ashtarot¦105169 and¦105170 at¦105169 Edrei¦105170,
\v 5 and ruled¦105172 over Mt¦105173. Hermon¦105174, Salekah¦105175, all¦105176 of Bashan¦105178 to the border of the Geshurites¦105182 and Maacathites¦105183, as well as half¦105184 of Gilead¦105185 to the border with¦105173 King¦105188 Sihon¦105187 from Heshbon¦105190.
\p
\v 6 Yahweh's¦105195 servant¦105193 Mosheh and the \add ≈Israelis¦105197\add* had \add ≈defeated¦105198 them¦105198\add* and Mosheh had given¦105199 \add @that region\add* as a possession¦105204 to the \add descendants of\add* Reuben and Gad and to the half-tribe of Menashsheh¦105209.\x + \xo 12:6: \xt Num 32:33; Deu 3:12.\x*
\s1 The kings defeated by Yehoshua
\rem /s1 Kings Defeated West of the Jordan; The Kings Defeated by Joshua; The Kings Conquered by Joshua
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 7 These¦105212 are¦105213 the kings¦105213 in the region that Yehoshua and¦105218 the \add ≈Israelis¦105219 defeated¦105216\add* on¦105220 the western side¦105220 of the Yordan¦105221 \add river\add* from¦105223 Baal-Gad¦105224 in the Lebanon¦105226 valley¦105225 to Mt¦105229. Halak¦105230 which¦105231 goes¦105231 up toward¦105232 Seir¦105232 \add !(Edom¦105232)\add*. Yehoshua \add ≈divided up\add* \add @that region\add* as a possession¦105237 to the \add various\add* tribes¦105235 of Yisrael¦105219,
\v 8 as well as the hill country¦105240, the lowlands¦105241, the \add ≈rift valley\add*, the slopes¦105243, the wilderness¦105244 and the Negev¦105245—\add the land of\add* the Hittites¦105246, Amorites¦105247, Canaanites¦105248, Perizzites¦105249, Hivites¦105250, and the Yebusites¦105251:
\v 9 the king of Yeriho¦105255 \add !(Jericho¦105255)\add*, the king of Ay¦105258 (near Beyt-El),
\v 10 the king of Yerushalem¦105268, the king of Hebron¦105271,
\v 11 the king of Yarmut, the king of Lakish,
\v 12 the king of Eglon¦105282, the king of Gezer¦105285,
\v 13 the king of Debir¦105289, the king of Geder¦105292,
\v 14 the king of Hormah¦105296, the king of Arad¦105299,
\v 15 the king of Libhah¦105303, the king of Adullam¦105306,
\v 16 the king of Makkedah¦105310, the king of Beyt-El,
\v 17 the king of Tappuah¦105319, the king of Hefer¦105322,
\v 18 the king of Afek¦105326, the king of Lasharon¦105329,
\v 19 the king of Madon¦105333, the king of Hatsor¦105336,
\v 20 the king of Shimron¦105341 Meron, the king of Akshaf,
\v 21 the king of Taanach¦105348, the king of Megiddo¦105351,
\v 22 the king of Kedesh¦105355, the king of Yokneam¦105359 in Karmel¦105360,
\v 23 the king of Dor of Nafoth Dor, the king of Goyim¦105370 in Gilgal¦105371,
