\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 8 \add ≈Along with¦105519 the other\add* \add half of\add* the half-tribe of Menashsheh, the \add ≈tribes of Reuben and¦105512 Gad\add* had¦105516 taken their¦105514 inheritance¦105514 on¦105519 the other (eastern¦105521) side¦105519 of the Yordan¦105520 as¦105522 \add ≈approved\add* by Yahweh's¦105527 servant¦105526 Mosheh¦105518,\x + \xo 13:8: \xt Num 32:33; Deu 3:12.\x*
\v 9 from Aroer, which¦105530 is¦105531 on¦105531 the edge¦105533 of the Arnon¦105536 riverbed¦105535, and the city¦105537 that's in¦105539 the middle¦105539 of the valley¦105541, and all¦105542 the plateau¦105544 \add ≈near\add* Medeba¦105545, to¦105546 Dibon¦105548.
\v 10 \add Also,\add* all¦105550 the cities¦105551 of King¦105553 Sihon¦105552 of the Amorites¦105554 who¦105555 ruled in¦105557 Heshbon¦105557, as far as the border¦105560 with¦105557 the Ammonites¦105562,
\v 11 and Gilead¦105564, and the territory¦105565 of¦105565 the Geshurites¦105566 and the Maacathites¦105567, and all Mt¦105569. Hermon¦105570, and all the Bashan¦105573 as far as Salekah¦105576,
\v 12 all the kingdom¦105580 of Og¦105581 in the Bashan¦105582, who¦105583 reigned¦105585 in Ashtaroth¦105586 and in Edrei¦105587 (what remained from the remnant¦105590 of the Refa'ites¦105591). Mosheh¦105593 \add ≈had¦105592 attacked them¦105592 and captured their lands\add*.
\v 13 \add ≈But¦105596\add* the \add ≈Israelis\add* didn't¦105596 \add ≈capture the land of\add* the Geshurites¦105607 or the Maacathites¦105608 and¦105596 \add ≈so those peoples¦105598\add* live \add ≈among the Israelis\add* to this¦105613 day¦105612.
\rem /s1 An Inheritance for the Tribe of Levi
\p
\v 14 The¦105616 only tribe that didn't¦105618 receive an¦105620 inheritance was the tribe of¦105621 Levi¦105617 because the offerings¦105621 given¦105619 to Yisrael's¦105624 god¦105623 Yahweh¦105622 are their¦105626 inheritance, just¦105627 like he'd told them.\x + \xo 13:14: \xt Deu 18:1.\x*
