\v 18 Yahaz, Kedemot¦105678, Mefaat,
\v 19 Kiriathaim, Sibmah¦105682, and¦105681 Zeret¦105683-Shahar on¦105685 the hill¦105685 \add ≈within\add* the valley¦105686.
\v 20 \add It also includes\add* Beyt-Peor, the slopes¦105690 of¦105690 the Pisgah¦105691, Beyt-Yeshimot,
\v 21 and all the cities¦105696 \add ≈on¦105706\add* the plateau¦105697, and all the kingdom¦105700 of Sihon (the king¦105702 of the Amorites¦105703 who had reigned¦105705 in Heshbon¦105706) who Mosheh¦105709 had \add ≈defeated¦105708\add*, he and the leaders¦105714 of Midian¦105715: Evi¦105718 and Rekem¦105721 and Zur¦105724 and Hur¦105727 and Reba¦105730 (the princes¦105731 of Sihon who had lived in the land¦105734).
\v 22 The \add ≈Israelis¦105746\add* also killed¦105743 Balaam¦105738 (Beor's¦105741 son¦105739 who practiced¦105742 divination¦105742) \add ≈along with¦105747 others\add*.
\v 23 The border¦105753 for Reuven's descendants was the Yordan¦105756 \add River\add*. So¦105752 that¦105758 was the inheritance¦105759 of¦105759 Reuven's descendants—all the cities¦105764 and¦105752 their villages¦105765 allocated to their clans¦105763.
