\p
\v 32 This was the land that¦105900 Mosheh¦105903 gave¦105902 as¦105902 an inheritance in¦105904 the plains¦105904 of Moab¦105905 on¦105904 the eastern¦105909 side¦105906 of the Yordan¦105907 \add River opposite\add* Yeriho¦105908 \add !(Jericho¦105908)\add*.
\v 33 \add ≈However,\add* Mosheh¦105917 didn't¦105914 give¦105916 any inheritance \add of land\add* to Levi's¦105913 descendants \add because\add* Yisrael's¦105921 god¦105920 Yahweh¦105919 is their¦105923 inheritance just¦105924 as¦105924 he¦105925 told them.\x + \xo 13:33: \xt Num 18:20; Deu 18:2.\x*
\c 14
\s1 The division of the main block west of the Yordan
\rem /s1 The Division of the Territory West of the Jordan; The Distribution of Territory West of the Jordan; Division of the Land West of the Jordan; The Land Divided West of the Jordan; Land distributed west of Jordan
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 These¦105928 are¦105929 what the \add ≈Israelis\add* inherited¦105931 in¦105935 the land¦105935 of Canaan¦105936, which¦105937 Eleazar¦105940 the priest¦105941 and Yehoshua (Nun's¦105945 son¦105943) and the \add ≈leaders\add* of the \add ≈Israelis\add* gave¦105938 them as an inheritance¦105931.
\v 2 Their \add ≈allocations were made by¦105957 casting lots\add* for¦105960 the¦105952 nine¦105960 and¦105962 a half¦105962 tribes¦105961, just¦105954 as¦105954 Yahweh¦105956 had¦105955 commanded¦105955 \add ≈through\add* Mosheh¦105959.\x + \xo 14:2: \xt Num 26:52-56; 34:13.\x*
\v 3 (Mosheh¦105968 had¦105967 given the other two¦105970 and a half tribes¦105971 their¦105981 inheritance on¦105981 the other side¦105974 of the river, but¦105972 the Levites¦105976 weren't given land as an¦105980 inheritance\x + \xo 14:3-4: \xt Num 32:33; 34:14-15; Deu 3:12-17.\x*—
\v 4 instead of¦105986 land they¦105985 were given¦105995 cities¦106002 to live¦106003 in, along with the \add surrounding\add* fields for¦106005 their¦106005 livestock¦106005. Yosef's¦105988 two sons Menashsheh¦105991 and¦106006 Efrayim¦105992 were considered as two tribes¦105990.)
\v 5 The \add ≈Israelis¦106017\add* did¦106015 just as Yahweh¦106010 had¦106009 commanded¦106009 Mosheh¦106013—they¦106015 allocated blocks of the¦106021 land¦106021 \add as permanent possessions\add*.
\s1 Hebron is allocated to Caleb
\rem /s1 Hebron Allotted to Caleb; Caleb Requests His Land; Hebron Is Given to Caleb; Hebron Given to Caleb
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 6 \add ≈Leaders from the tribe of\add* Yehudah¦106027 approached¦106024 Yehoshua at Gilgal¦106031 and Caleb¦106034 (son¦106035 of Yefunneh¦106037 the Kenizzite¦106038) said¦106032 to him, “You yourself know¦106040 what Yahweh¦106047 told the man¦106051 of God¦106053 Mosheh¦106050 at Kadesh-Barnea about¦106056 me and you.\x + \xo 14:6: \xt Num 14:30.\x*
\v 7 I was¦106061 \add ≈forty¦106063 years old\add* when¦106066 Yahweh's¦106070 servant¦106068 Mosheh¦106067 sent¦106066 me¦106071 from¦106072 Kadesh-Barnea to¦106074 spy¦106074 out¦106074 the¦106077 land¦106077, and¦106078 I brought¦106078 back¦106078 \add ≈an honest report\add*.\x + \xo 14:7: \xt Num 13:1-30.\x*
\v 8 \add ≈The other men\add* who went¦106088 made the \add ≈people¦106094 terrified\add*, \add ≈but¦106086\add* I \add ≈remained loyal to\add* my¦106099 god¦106099 Yahweh¦106098.
\v 9 Mosheh¦106102 \add ≈promised me\add* that day¦106103, saying¦106105, ‘The land¦106109 \add ≈that you walked on¦106113\add* will certainly be for an¦106116 inheritance¦106116 for you and¦106101 your¦106117 sons \add ≈forever¦106120\add*, because¦106121 you were \add ≈completely loyal to\add* my¦106125 god¦106125 Yahweh¦106124.’\x + \xo 14:9: \xt Num 14:24.\x*
\v 10 Now¦106127, listen. Yahweh has¦106129 kept me¦106132 alive these forty-five¦106136 years since Yahweh said that¦106135 to¦106146 Mosheh¦106148, \add back\add* when¦106149 Yisrael¦106152 was walking¦106151 in¦106153 the wilderness¦106153. \add ≈Yes, believe it¦106151 or not, I'm now¦106154 eighty-five¦106161.\add*
\v 11 I'm still as strong¦106166 today as \add I was\add* on¦106168 the day¦106168 that Mosheh¦106171 sent¦106169 me¦106170. \add ≈Just like I could fight back then¦106173, I can still fight or travel just the same\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈So\add* now, please give¦106181 me that hill¦106186 country¦106186 that Yahweh \add ≈promised\add* that day, because¦106194 you yourself heard¦106197 \add ≈me say\add* that the Anakim¦106202 lived there¦106203 in¦106198 fortified¦106206 cities¦106204. \add So now,\add* perhaps¦106207 Yahweh will help me to take them¦106210 over just¦106211 as¦106211 \add *he¦106212\add* said.”
\p
\v 13 \add ≈So¦106215\add* Yehoshua¦106216 blessed¦106215 Yefunneh's¦106224 son¦106222 \add @Caleb¦106221\add* and¦106217 gave¦106217 him¦106215 Hebron¦106220 as his inheritance¦106225.
\v 14 Because¦106242 of that¦106241, Hebron¦106232 belongs¦106230 to Caleb¦106233 (Yefunneh¦106236 the¦106234 Kenizzite's¦106237 son¦106234) as an¦106238 inheritance¦106238 until¦106239 this¦106241 day¦106240, because¦106242 he¦106244 was \add ≈completely loyal to\add* Yisrael's¦106248 god¦106247 Yahweh¦106246.
\v 15 (Hebron¦106251 used to be called Kiriat¦106254-Arba—\add @Arba\add* had been a \add ≈brave warrior\add* among¦106257 the Anakim¦106257.)
\p Then¦106250 there was¦106260 a time of no more war¦106261 in¦106257 that region.
\c 15
\s1 The area assigned to Yehudah's descendants
\rem /s1 The Territory of Judah; The Land Given to the Tribe of Judah; Allotment for Judah; The Territory Assigned to Judah
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 \add This was the land\add* that was assigned to Yehudah's¦106268 descendants¦106267 according to their¦106269 clans¦106269:
\p It went from the Zin¦106276 wilderness¦106274 in the south¦106277 to¦106269 the border¦106272 with Edom¦106273,
\v 2 and¦106281 their southern border¦106283 was¦106281 the south-facing bay at the end¦106285 of the \add ≈Dead Sea\add* \add (also called the Salt Sea)\add*.
\v 3 \add From there\add* it went south¦106297 of the Scorpion¦106299 Pass, across to Zin¦106301, \add ≈climbed\add* up to Kadesh-Barnea, crossed to Hezron¦106307, went to Addar¦106309, and¦106294 around to Karka¦106311.
\v 4 Then¦106313 it¦106325 crosses to Azmon¦106314 and out¦106315 to the Egyptian riverbed¦106316 and \add ≈finishes\add* at¦106322 the \add Mediterranean\add* sea¦106322. That will¦106325 be¦106325 their southern¦106328 border¦106327.
\p
\v 5 The¦106338 eastern border¦106330 was the \add ≈Dead Sea¦106342\add* as far as the end¦106336 of¦106336 the Yordan¦106337.
\p The northern¦106340 border \add starts\add* at the top of the \add ≈Dead Sea\add* where the Yordan \add river\add* enters it
\v 6 then¦106346 to Beyt-Hoglah¦106349 and¦106346 \add further\add* north¦106351 to Beyt-Aravah to the Stone¦106356 of Bohan¦106357 (Reuben's¦106360 son¦106360).
\v 7 Then¦106362 the border went¦106362 to Debir¦106365 from the Akor Valley¦106366, and to the north¦106368, turning¦106369 to the Gilgal¦106372, which is in front of the Adummim¦106377 pass which is from the south¦106379 of the riverbed¦106380, then¦106362 the border passed¦106381 over to the waters¦106385 of Eyn-Shemesh and its¦106390 ends¦106390 at Eyn-Rogel¦106394.
\v 8 \add ≈From there\add* the border went up the valley of Ben¦106398 Hinnom to the edge of the Yebusite¦106405 region from¦106406 the south¦106406 (that¦106415 is Yerushalem¦106408). Then¦106396 the border went to the head of the hill¦106414 opposite the Hinnom valley to the west, which¦106423 is at¦106424 the end¦106424 of the valley of the Refa'ites to the north¦106428.
\v 9 \add ≈From there\add* the border turned from¦106432 the head of the hill¦106433 to the Neftoah spring¦106436 and¦106430 went¦106439 out¦106439 to the cities¦106442 of Mt¦106433. Efron¦106445, then¦106430 the border turned to Ba'alah (\add ≈now called\add* Kiriat¦106451-Yearim).
\v 10 Then¦106453 the border¦106454 went around from Ba'alah to the west to Mt. Seir¦106460, and passed over to the shoulder of Mt. Yearim¦106467 from the north¦106468 (\add ≈also called\add* Kesalon¦106470), and went down¦106471 to Beyt-Shemesh¦106474, and passed over to Timnah¦106476.
\v 11 \add ≈From there\add* the border went out to the shoulder of¦106482 Ekron¦106483 to the north¦106484, then turned¦106485 toward Shikkeron¦106487 and passed¦106488 over to Mt¦106489. Baalah¦106491, and went out to Yabneel, then the border ended at the sea¦106497.
\v 12 The western border¦106499 was the \add ≈Mediterranean\add* Sea¦106501. Those were the borders of¦106505 \add the land given to\add* Yehudah's¦106508 descendants¦106506 to be allocated to their¦106510 clans¦106510.
\s1 Caleb defeats Hebron and Debir
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Caleb; Caleb Occupies His Portion; Caleb Conquers Hebron and Debir
\s4 Promised land
\r (Jdg. 1:11-15)
\p
\v 13 Yahweh¦106525 had instructed Yehoshua to give¦106516 \add this\add* block of land to Caleb (Yefunneh's¦106515 son¦106513): Kiriat¦106529-Arba (\add ≈now called\add* Hebron¦106534—Arba was Anak's¦106532 father¦106531).\x + \xo 15:13-14: \xt Jdg 1:20.\x*
\v 14 Caleb¦106538 captured \add the land\add* from Anak's¦106543 three¦106541 sons¦106542—Sheshai¦106546, Ahiman¦106549, and¦106536 Talmai¦106552,
\v 15 then¦106556 from there¦106557, he \add ≈battled against¦106558\add* Debir¦106561 (formerly¦106565 called Kiriat¦106568-Sefer¦106564)
\v 16 and \add *he¦106570\add* said¦106570, “I'll¦106581 give¦106581 my daughter¦106586 Aksah to marry \add ≈to the¦106572 man who¦106572 attacks¦106574\add* Kiriat¦106577-Sefer and captures¦106580 it.”
\v 17 Then¦106589 Othniel¦106590 (Kenaz's¦106593 son¦106591 and¦106596 Caleb's¦106595 brother¦106594) captured¦106589 \add @the city\add*, \add ≈so\add* Caleb gave¦106596 his daughter¦106602 Aksah to him for¦106603 a wife.
\v 18 Then¦106605 \add ≈when¦106606 she married him\add*, she \add ≈encouraged\add* him to ask¦106608 her father¦106611 for a field¦106612, \add ≈so\add* she got down¦106613 off her donkey¦106615 and¦106605 Caleb¦106619 asked, “What¦106620 \add ≈are you¦106622 up to\add*?”
\v 19 “Give¦106625 me a blessing¦106628,” she¦106624 answered, “because¦106629 you've¦106632 given¦106632 me land¦106630 in the Negev¦106631 \add desert region\add*, \add ≈so now\add* give¦106633 me some springs \add as well\add* for water¦106636.” \add ≈So¦106624\add* he gave¦106637 her¦106639 \add both\add* the upper¦106642 and¦106624 the lower¦106645 springs.
\s1 Cities captured by Yehudah's descendants
\rem /s1 The Towns Judah Inherited; The Cities of Judah; The Towns of Judah
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 20 This¦106648 is Yehudah's¦106653 inheritance¦106649 according to¦106654 their¦106654 clans¦106654:
\v 21 The cities¦106657 at¦106667 the edge of Yehudah's¦106662 block toward the border¦106665 with¦106667 Edom¦106666 in¦106667 Negev were Kabzeel¦106668, Eder¦106669, Yagur,
\v 22 Kinah¦106672, Dimonah¦106673, Adadah¦106674,
\v 23 Kedesh, Hatsor, Ithnan¦106678,
\v 24 Zif, Telem¦106681, Bealot¦106682,
\v 25 Hatsor-Hadattah, Keriot¦106687-Hezron¦106688 (\add ≈also called\add* Hatsor),
\v 26 Amam, Shema¦106693, Molodah,
\v 27 Hazar¦106696-Gaddah, Heshmon¦106698, Beyt-Pelet,
\v 28 Hazar¦106702-Shual, Be'er-Sheva, and¦106702 Biziothiah¦106706,
\v 29 Baalah¦106708, Iyim¦106709, Etsem¦106710,
\v 30 Eltolad¦106712, Kesil¦106713, Hormah¦106714,
\v 31 Ziklag¦106716, Madmannah¦106717, Sansannah¦106718,
\v 32 Lebaot¦106720, Shilhim¦106721, Ain¦106722, and¦106720 Rimmon¦106723—\add ≈a total¦106724 of\add* twenty-nine¦106727 cities¦106726 as well as their¦106729 villages¦106729.
\p
\v 33 \add Then down\add* in¦106732 the lowlands¦106732 were Eshtaol¦106733, Zorah¦106734, Ashnah¦106735,
\v 34 Zanoah¦106737, Eyn-Gannim, Tappuah¦106740, Enam,
\v 35 Yarmut, Adullam¦106744, Sokoh, Azekah¦106746,
\v 36 Shaaraim¦106748, Adithaim¦106749, and¦106748 Gederah¦106750 (\add also called\add* Gederothaim¦106751)—\add ≈a total of¦106756\add* fourteen cities¦106752 as well as their¦106756 \add surrounding\add* villages¦106756.
\p
\v 37 \add Also\add* Zenan¦106758, Hadashah¦106759, Migdal¦106760-Gad¦106762,
\v 38 Dilean¦106764, Mizpah¦106765, Yoktheel¦106766,
\v 39 Lachish, Bozkat¦106769, Eglon¦106770,
\v 40 Kabbon, Lahmas¦106773, Kitlish¦106774,
\v 41 Gederot¦106776, Beyt¦106777-Dagon¦106779, Naamah¦106780, and¦106776 Makkedah¦106781—sixteen cities¦106782 as well as their¦106786 villages¦106786.
\p
\v 42 \add Also\add* Libnah¦106789, Ether¦106790, Ashan¦106791,
\v 43 Yiftah¦106793, Ashnah¦106794, Nezib¦106795,
\v 44 Keilah¦106797, Akzib¦106798, and¦106797 Maresha¦106799—nine¦106801 cities¦106800 as well as their¦106802 villages¦106802.
\p
\v 45 \add Also\add* Ekron with its¦106805 towns¦106805 and¦106806 villages¦106806
\v 46 from Ekron to¦106809 the¦106815 \add ≈Mediterranean\add*—\add ≈those near\add* Ashdod¦106816 and¦106817 their¦106817 villages¦106817.
\p
\v 47 \add Also\add* Ashdod and its towns and its villages, Gaza¦106822 and its towns and its villages, as far as the riverbed¦106827 of¦106827 Egypt¦106828 and the \add ≈Mediterranean\add* sea¦106829 and the border.
\p
\v 48 \add Also\add* in¦106835 the hill country¦106835: Shamir¦106836, Yattir¦106837, Socoh¦106838,
\v 49 Dannah¦106840, Kiriat-Sannah (\add ≈also called\add* Debir¦106845),
\v 50 Anab, Eshtemoh¦106848, Anim,
\v 51 Goshen¦106851, Holon¦106852, and¦106851 Giloh¦106853—eleven cities¦106854 as well as their¦106858 villages¦106858.
\p
\v 52 \add Also\add* Arab, Dumah¦106861, Eshan¦106862,
\v 53 Yanim¦106864, Beyt-Tappuah, Afekah,
\v 54 Humtah¦106871, and Kiriat-Arba (\add ≈also called\add* Hebron¦106875) and Zior—nine¦106878 cities¦106877 as well as their¦106879 villages¦106879.
\p
\v 55 \add Also\add* Maon¦106882, Karmel¦106884, Zif¦106885, Yuttah,
\v 56 Yezreel, Yokdeam¦106889, Zanoah¦106890,
\v 57 Kayin, Gibeah¦106893, and Timnah¦106894—ten¦106896 cities¦106895 as well as their¦106897 villages¦106897.
\p
\v 58 \add Also\add* Halhul¦106899, Beyt-Zur¦106902, Gedor¦106903,
\v 59 Maarat¦106905, Beyt-Anot, and¦106905 Eltekon¦106909—six¦106911 cities¦106910 as well as their¦106912 villages¦106912.
\p
\v 60 \add Also\add* Kiriat-Baal¦106916 (\add ≈also called\add* Kiriat-Yearim¦106919) and Rabbah¦106920—two¦106922 cities¦106921 as well as their¦106923 villages¦106923.
\p
\v 61 In¦106926 the wilderness¦106926, Beyt¦106927-Aravah¦106928, Middin¦106929, Secacah¦106930,
\v 62 Nibshan¦106932, the City¦106933 of Salt, and¦106932 Eyn-Gedi—six¦106939 cities¦106938 as well as their¦106940 villages¦106940.
\p
\v 63 \add ≈But¦106942\add* Yehudah's¦106953 descendants weren't able to defeat the Yebusites¦106944 who lived in¦106961 Yerushalem¦106946, so \add *they¦106949\add* have lived among the tribe of¦106959 Yehudah to this¦106964 day¦106963.\x + \xo 15:63: \xt Jdg 1:21; 2Sam 5:6; 1Ch 11:4.\x*
\c 16
\s1 The allocation to Yosef's descendants
\rem /s1 Allotment for Ephraim and Manasseh; The Inheritance of Ephraim and West Manasseh; The Territory Assigned to Ephraim and West Manasseh; The Territory of Ephraim
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 The block for Yosef's¦106970 descendants¦106969\f + \fr 16:1 \ft i.e., the half-tribes of Efrayim and Menashsheh.\f* went¦106967 from the Yordan¦106971 at¦106979 Yeriho¦106974 (\add Jericho\add*, east of the \add ≈springs\add*), through the wilderness¦106976 into the hill country¦106979 of Beyt-El.
\v 2 It¦106984 went¦106984 out¦106984 from¦106985 Beyt-El to Luz¦106988 then¦106984 along¦106989 the border¦106992 with the Arkites¦106993 at Atarot¦106994.
\v 3 Then¦106996 it¦107013 went¦106996 west to the border with the Yafletites as far as the border with Lower¦107008 Beyt-Horon¦107007 and¦106996 as far as Gezer¦107011, then¦106996 out to the \add ≈Mediterranean\add*.
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Ephraim
\p
\v 4 \add ≈So¦107017\add* Yosef's¦107020 sons Menashsheh¦107021 and¦107022 Efrayim¦107022 received¦107017 an inheritance¦107017.
\s1 The allocation to Efrayim's descendants
\rem /s1 Ephraim
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 5 The allotment for Efrayim's¦107028 descendants¦107026 according to¦107029 their¦107029 clans¦107029 was¦107030 at Atarot¦107034-Addar¦107035 in the¦107031 east, going as far as Upper¦107040 Beyt-Horon¦107039
\v 6 and¦107042 out¦107042 to the \add ≈Mediterranean\add*. From¦107046 Mikmetat in the north¦107046, the border¦107048 went¦107042 eastward¦107049 toward Taanat¦107050-Shiloh¦107051 then¦107042 further east¦107054 to Yanoah¦107055.
\v 7 From Yanoah¦107058 it went¦107057 to Atarot¦107059 and¦107057 Naarah¦107060, reached Yeriho¦107062 \add !(Jericho¦107062)\add* then¦107057 came¦107063 out¦107063 at¦107062 the¦107064 Yordan¦107064.
\v 8 \add The northern border went\add* from Tappuah to the Kanah¦107071 riverbed¦107070 and¦107072 then out to the \add ≈Mediterranean\add*. That was¦107076 the inheritance¦107076 of Efrayim's¦107080 descendants¦107078 according to their¦107081 clans¦107081,
\v 9 \add ≈although\add* some of the cities¦107083 with their¦107095 villages¦107095 for¦107085 Efrayim's¦107086 descendants were \add actually\add* inside the territory assigned to Menashsheh's¦107091 descendants.
\v 10 \add ≈But¦107097\add* they didn't¦107097 \add ≈capture the land of\add* the Canaanites¦107101 who lived in¦107103 Gezer¦107103, so they've lived within Efrayim¦107107 to this¦107111 day¦107110 and¦107097 were forced¦107113 to serve as labourers¦107113.\x + \xo 16:10: \xt Jdg 1:29.\x*
\c 17
\s1 The allocation to Menashsheh's descendants
\rem /s1 The Land Given to West Manasseh; West Manasseh; The Other Half-Tribe of Manasseh (West)
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 The allotment for Menashsheh's¦107121 descendants (Yosef's¦107126 eldest son) \add included a special allotment for\add* (Gilead's¦107131 father¦107130) Makir¦107127—he was given Gilead and¦107137 Bashan¦107141 because¦107122 he was a \add ≈powerful warrior\add*.
\v 2 The¦107144 other Menashsheh clans \add that were allocated land\add* were the Abiezer¦107149, Helek¦107152, Asriel¦107154, Shekem¦107157, Hefer¦107160, and¦107143 Shemida¦107162 clans. (They were the sons of Yosef's son¦107166 Menashsheh \add who led their own\add* clans.)
\v 3 \add ≈But¦107172\add* Zelofehad (son of Hefer¦107175, son of Gilead¦107178, son of Makir¦107181, son of Menashsheh¦107184) had no sons¦107189—only daughters¦107193 who were named Mahlah¦107197, Noah¦107198, Hoglah¦107199, Milkah, and¦107172 Tirzah¦107201.
\v 4 They¦107203 approached the priest¦107206 Eleazar and Yehoshua and the other leaders¦107214 and said¦107215, “Yahweh told¦107217 Mosheh¦107220 to give¦107221 us¦107223 an inheritance along with our¦107226 brothers¦107226.” \add ≈So¦107203\add* he\f + \fr 17:4 \ft It's not clear who this ‘he’ refers to here—some translations choose Eleazar (implied by the sentence structure) and others choose Yehoshua (implied by past allocations of land).\f* gave¦107227 them an inheritance (like he'd given their¦107236 uncles), as Yahweh \add ≈had instructed¦107217 them\add*.\x + \xo 17:4: \xt Num 27:1-7.\x*
\v 5 \add ≈So¦107238\add* ten¦107242 blocks were allocated to Menashsheh¦107241 \add tribe\add* as well as Gilead¦107245 and¦107238 Bashan¦107246 which¦107247 were across the Yordan¦107249
\v 6 because¦107251 Menashsheh's daughters¦107252 received inheritances¦107254 along with his sons. The¦107258 land¦107258 of Gilead¦107259 belonged¦107260 to¦107261 the¦107261 rest of Menashsheh's sons.
\p
\v 7 The¦107267 border¦107267 for Menashsheh¦107269 went from¦107270 Asher¦107270 to Mikmetat \add ≈opposite\add* Shekem¦107276, then¦107266 went \add ≈south¦107281\add* towards the spring at Tappuah.
\v 8 (The Tappuah \em land¦107290\em* was for Menashsheh¦107296, but¦107292 Tappuah \add town\add* was for Efrayim¦107298.)
\v 9 Then¦107300 the border went¦107300 south¦107304 to the Kanah¦107303 riverbed—the cities there belonged¦107308 to Efrayim¦107308 even though they were inside Menashsheh's¦107311 land—then¦107300 the border stayed on the north¦107314 side of the riverbed and¦107300 extended to the \add ≈Mediterranean¦107313\add*.
\v 10 \add So\add* the south was for Efrayim¦107321 and the north was for Menashsheh¦107323, and the sea¦107325 was the \add western\add* border¦107326, meeting Asher¦107327 from the north and Yissakar from the east¦107331.
\v 11 Menashsheh¦107334 was¦107333 allocated cities inside \add both\add* Yissakar's and Asher's¦107336 territories: Beyt-Shan, Ibleam¦107341, Dor¦107346, Endor¦107351, Taanach¦107354, and Megiddo¦107357 along with¦107335 their \add ≈surrounding towns\add*.\f + \fr 17:11 \ft We've omitted the final Hebrew phrase here (the three of Nafet) since it's unclear what it means (plus it's not considered to be a vital point in the narrative).\f*
\v 12 \add ≈But¦107362\add* Menashsheh's¦107365 descendants¦107364 weren't able¦107363 to take¦107366 possession¦107366 of¦107366 those cities¦107369, \add ≈so\add* the Canaanites¦107372 continued to live¦107373 in the region.\x + \xo 17:12-13: \xt Jdg 1:27-28.\x*
\v 13 \add ≈When¦107377 the¦107380 Israelis¦107381 strengthened their position\add*, they were able to force¦107386 those Canaanites¦107385 to work for them, \add ≈but¦107377\add* they weren't able to \add ≈drive them out\add*.
\s1 Efrayim and Menashsheh's descendants are given additional land
\rem /s1 The Tribe of Joseph Protests; Ephraim and West Manasseh Request More Land
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 14 Then the¦107393 \add two\add* \add ≈half-tribes of Efrayim and¦107405 Menashsheh\add* asked Yehoshua, “Why¦107399 have¦107400 you¦107400 \add only\add* given¦107400 to¦107401 \add #us\add* one¦107406 measured allocation as an¦107402 inheritance¦107402 when \add #we're\add* \add very\add* numerous¦107410 \add because\add* Yahweh¦107418 has¦107417 \add ≈already\add* blessed¦107417 \add #us\add*?”
\p
\v 15 “If¦107423 \add ≈there's so many of you\add*,” Yehoshua¦107422 \add ≈answered\add*, “and if Efrayim's¦107444 hill-country is too small for you, go¦107429 into the forested¦107431 area of the Perizzites¦107436 and the Refaites¦107437 and clear¦107432 some land¦107435 for yourselves¦107441 there.”
\p
\v 16 “The¦107447 hill¦107453 country¦107453 \add certainly\add* isn't¦107449 big enough for \add all of\add* us,” \add *they¦107446\add* responded¦107446, “plus¦107454 the Canaanites¦107458 living in the Yezreel¦107470 valley¦107462 and in Beyt-Shan and the surrounding towns have iron¦107455 chariots¦107454.”
\p
\v 17 \add ≈So¦107472\add* Yehoshua told the¦107476 \add ≈half-tribes of Efrayim¦107478 and Menashsheh¦107479\add*, “\add Yes\add*, there's a lot¦107492 of you and you're very powerful¦107485. One land allotment \add ≈wouldn't be enough for you\add*
\v 18 \add ≈so\add* the hill¦107496 country¦107496 will be yours¦107506 \add as well\add*. \add ≈However\add*, it's a forest¦107502 and you'll have to clear¦107504 it to the borders¦107507. You'll \add need to\add* drive out the Canaanites¦107513 even if¦107518 they are strong¦107519 and with iron¦107516 chariots¦107515.”
\c 18
\s1 Allocations for the remaining seven tribes
\rem /s1 The Territories of the Remaining Tribes; Division of the Rest of the Land; The Allotments of the Remaining Land; The Division of the Rest of the Land
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then all¦107524 the Israelis¦107529 assembled¦107523 at Shiloh¦107530 and set up the sacred¦107535 tent¦107535 there¦107532. The \add ≈battles over the land had stopped\add*
\v 2 but¦107541 seven¦107551 of \add *their\add* tribes¦107552 hadn't had¦107547 their inheritances¦107550 assigned \add yet\add*.
\v 3 Yehoshua asked the Israelis¦107559, “\add ≈How much longer are you all going¦107565 to put off capturing\add* the land¦107569 that¦107570 your ancestors' God¦107574 Yahweh¦107573 has¦107571 given¦107571 you?
\v 4 Choose three¦107579 men¦107580 from each \add of those seven\add*\f + \fr 18:4 \ft Not in the Hebrew but implied by verse 5 as they go on to divide the surveyed land into seven portions.\f* tribes¦107581 and I'll send¦107582 them out to \add ≈scout around\add* \add and inspect\add* the land and write¦107586 \add ≈descriptions¦107586 of it in terms of potential allocations and bring it\add* to me¦107591.
\v 5 They¦107593 can divide¦107593 \add @that land\add* into¦107595 seven¦107595 parts. (Yehudah¦107597 will¦107598 maintain their¦107608 territory¦107601 in the south¦107602, and¦107603 Yosef's¦107604 tribes in the north¦107609.)
\v 6 You all should write¦107612 descriptions¦107612 of the seven parts and bring¦107618 them here to me¦107619, and in front¦107625 of our¦107627 god¦107627 Yahweh¦107626, I'll¦107621 throw¦107621 dice for you \add to allocate them to the seven tribes\add*.
\v 7 However, the Levites¦107633 don't¦107630 receive a portion¦107632, because¦107635 their inheritance is Yahweh's priesthood¦107637. Gad¦107640 and Reuven and the Menashsheh¦107644 half-tribe have¦107645 \add already\add* received¦107645 their inheritance that¦107650 Yahweh's servant¦107654 Mosheh¦107653 allocated to them¦107652 on¦107634 the eastern¦107649 side¦107647 of¦107654 the Yordan¦107648.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈So¦107657\add* the \add chosen\add* men¦107658 \add ≈got ready to leave\add* and Yehoshua instructed¦107660 them, “Go and walk¦107671 around that land¦107668 and write¦107673 \add a report\add* and \add ≈bring it back\add* to me¦107676. Then¦107657 I'll¦107678 throw¦107678 dice for¦107679 you all \add ≈in front¦107681\add* of¦107681 Yahweh¦107682 here in Shiloh¦107683.”
\v 9 Then¦107685 the men¦107686 left and¦107685 \add ≈walked through the area\add*, writing¦107689 down \add their recommendations\add* for dividing the seven¦107691 portions¦107692 according to the cities¦107690 \add in the area\add*, then¦107685 they¦107696 returned back to Yehoshua¦107699 at the camp¦107702 at Shiloh¦107703.
\v 10 \add ≈So¦107705\add* Yehoshua threw¦107705 dice for¦107706 them¦107706 at Shiloh¦107709 \add ≈in front¦107710\add* of Yahweh¦107711, and¦107705 \add ≈so that land¦107718 was allocated to those remaining seven tribes\add*.
\s1 The allocation to Benyamin's descendants
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Benjamin; The Territory of Benjamin; Allotment for Benjamin; The Territory Assigned to Benjamin
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 11 The¦107725 tribe¦107726 of¦107725 Benyamin¦107729 won the \add first\add* draw and the area for their clans¦107730 was between¦107734 the land assigned to Yehudah¦107736 and that assigned to \add ≈Efrayim and Menashsheh\add*.
\v 12 Their northern border¦107743 went from the Yordan¦107748 then¦107741 to the northern side¦107744 of Yeriho¦107754 \add !(Jericho¦107754)\add* and¦107741 up¦107749 into the hill country¦107757 to the west, coming¦107759 out in¦107757 the wilderness¦107762 at¦107757 Beyt-Aven.
\v 13 Then¦107766 it¦107766 went¦107779 across towards Luz¦107769 (\add ≈now called\add* Beyt-El) to the southern edge then¦107766 downhill towards Atarot¦107781-Addar¦107782 beside the hill¦107785 south¦107787 of¦107788 lower¦107791 Beyt-Horon.
\v 14 Then¦107793 the western border¦107794 turned from¦107800 that¦107803 hill¦107802 and¦107793 went¦107811 south¦107810, coming out at Kiriat-Baal¦107818 (\add ≈also called\add* Kiriat-Yearim¦107821—a town¦107822 belonging to Yehudah¦107824) thus forming the western side¦107826.
\v 15 The southern¦107832 border¦107837 went¦107839 west from¦107833 Kiriat¦107835-Yearim to the spring¦107842 at Neftoah,
\v 16 then downhill to the Ben¦107856-Hinnon valley (in¦107861 the valley of the Refaites¦107862 to the north¦107863) then downhill to Hinnon valley to the edge of the Yebusites¦107870 and¦107846 downhill to Eyn-Rogel¦107874.
\v 17 Then¦107876 it turned¦107876 northward¦107877 and went¦107878 \add west\add* to Eyn-Shemesh¦107880 and across to Gelilot¦107884 opposite¦107887 the Adummim¦107889 pass, before going downhill to the Stone¦107891 of Bohan¦107892 (Reuben's¦107895 son¦107895).
\v 18 It¦107897 extended over to¦107898 the northern¦107904 slope¦107900 of¦107900 the Yordan valley and¦107905 then¦107897 downhill into the \add actual\add* valley.
\v 19 \add *It¦107908\add* then¦107908 went¦107917 \add east\add* to the northern slope¦107912 of Beyt-Hoglah¦107915 before coming out at¦107929 the \add ≈north end¦107932\add* of the \add ≈Dead Sea\add* \add (also called the Salt Sea)\add* where the Yordan¦107933 river flows into it¦107908. That was the southern boundary¦107922
\v 20 and¦107939 the Yordan¦107939 borders it¦107942 on the east. Those were the borders of¦107950 Benyamin's¦107949 descendants' inheritance¦107947 according¦107950 to¦107952 their¦107952 clans¦107952.
\rem /s1 The Towns Given to Benjamin
\p
\v 21 The cities¦107955 allocated to Benyamin's¦107958 descendants¦107957 and¦107954 their¦107959 clans¦107959 were: Yeriho¦107960 \add !(Jericho¦107960)\add*, Beyt-Hoglah, Emek-Keziz,
\v 22 Beyt-Aravah, Zemaraim¦107969, Beyt-El,
\v 23 Avvim¦107974, Parah¦107975, Ofrah¦107976,
\v 24 Kefar-Ammoni¦107978, Ofni, and¦107978 Geba¦107982—a total of¦107987 twelve cities¦107983 as well as their¦107987 \add surrounding\add* villages¦107987.
\v 25 \add Also\add* Gibeon, Ramah¦107990, Beerot¦107991,
\v 26 Mizpah, Kefirah¦107994, Mozah¦107995,
\v 27 Rekem¦107997, Irpeel¦107998, Taralah¦107999,
\v 28 Zelah, Haelef¦108002, Yebus¦108003 (\add ≈now called\add* Yerushalem¦108006), Gibeah¦108007, and¦108001 Kiriat¦108008—\add a total of\add* fourteen cities¦108009 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108013. Those were Benyamin's¦108018 descendants' inheritance¦108015 according to¦108019 their clans¦108019.
\c 19
\s1 The allocation to Shimeon's descendants
\rem /s1 The Territory Assigned to Simeon; The Land Given to Simeon; The Territory of Simeon; Allotment for Simeon
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 The second¦108024 draw went¦108022 to Shimeon's (Simeon's¦108025) descendants and¦108031 the land for their¦108030 clans¦108030 was¦108031 in¦108033 the middle¦108033 of¦108037 Yehudah's¦108037 territory.
\v 2 Shimeon's inheritance¦108041 \add ≈included\add*: Beer¦108042-Sheba,\f + \fr 19:2 \ft TC: Ancient manuscripts differ, with some adding Sheba (possibly a mistaken reduplication) or Shema here (but that would make the total number wrong that's given in v6).\f* Moladah¦108046,\x + \xo 19:2-8: \xt 1Ch 4:28-33.\x*
\v 3 Hazarshual¦108048, Balah¦108050, Ezem¦108051,
\v 4 Eltolad, Betul¦108054, Hormah¦108055,
\v 5 Ziklag¦108057, Beyt-Markabot. Hatsarsusah,
\v 6 Beyt-Lebaot, and¦108064 Sharuhen¦108066—thirteen cities¦108067 as well as their¦108071 \add surrounding\add* villages¦108071.
\p
\v 7 \add Also\add* Ain, Rimmon¦108075, Eter¦108076, and Asha—four¦108079 cities¦108078 as well as their¦108080 \add surrounding\add* villages¦108080,
\v 8 and¦108082 all¦108082 the \add further\add* villages¦108084 around¦108086 those cities¦108087 as far as Baalat-Beer¦108092 (\add also called\add* Ramah¦108093 of¦108086 the Negev¦108094). That was¦108096 Shimeon's descendants' inheritance¦108096 according to¦108101 their¦108101 clans¦108101.
\v 9 This \add took away\add* some of Yehudah's inheritance¦108106 and¦108118 gave it¦108111 to Shimeons descendants because¦108109 Yehudah's \add initial\add* area was¦108111 more than \add ≈they¦108118 needed\add*.
\s1 The allocation to Zebulun's descendants
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Zebulun; The Territory of Zebulun; Allotment for Zebulun; The Territory Assigned to Zebulun
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 10 The third¦108128 draw went to Zebulun's¦108130 descendants¦108129 according to their clans¦108131. The \add southern\add* border¦108133 for their inheritance¦108134 \add ≈started\add* at Sarid¦108137
\v 11 and went¦108139 \add west\add* to Maralah¦108143 and Dabbeshet¦108145 then¦108139 to the riverbed¦108149 facing Yokneam¦108154.
\v 12 \add Also\add* from Sarid¦108157 it went toward the east beside the border¦108163 with Kislot¦108165-Tabor and then on to Daberat¦108169 and then to Yafia¦108171.
\v 13 From¦108173 there¦108173 it¦108174 extended east to Gittah-Hefer¦108178 and Ittah-Katsin and \add north\add* to Rimmon¦108182 before turning¦108183 to Neah.
\v 14 Then¦108186 \add *it\add* passed north¦108189 of Hannaton¦108190 ending at Yiftah¦108194-El¦108196 valley¦108193.
\v 15 \add It included the cities of\add* Kattat¦108198, Nahalal¦108199, Shimron¦108200, Idalah¦108201, and¦108198 Bethlehem—\add a total of\add* twelve cities as well as their¦108208 \add surrounding\add* villages¦108208.
\v 16 That was¦108211 Zebulun's¦108214 descendants' inheritance¦108211 according¦108215 to¦108215 their clans¦108215, \add including\add* those cities¦108216 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108218.
\s1 The allocation to Yissakar's descendants
\rem /s1 The Territory Assigned to Issachar; Allotment for Issachar; The Territory of Issachar; The Land Given to Issachar
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 17 The fourth¦108224 draw went¦108222 to Yissakar's descendants¦108225 according¦108227 to their¦108227 clans¦108227.
\v 18 \add ≈Their¦108230 land\add* \add included the cities of\add* Yezreel¦108231, Kesulot¦108232, Shunem¦108233,
\v 19 Hafaraim, Shion¦108236, Anaharat¦108237,
\v 20 Rabbit¦108239, Kishion¦108240, Ebets¦108241,
\v 21 Remet¦108243, Eyn-Gannim, Eyn-Haddah, and¦108243 Beyt-Pazzets.
\v 22 The border¦108253 \add of their allotment\add* met with¦108254 Tabor¦108254, Shahazumah¦108255, and¦108252 Beyt-Shemesh, coming out \add in the east\add* at¦108254 the Yordan¦108262—\add a total of\add* sixteen cities¦108263 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108267.
\v 23 That was¦108270 Yissakar's descendants' inheritance¦108270 according to¦108275 their clans¦108275, \add including\add* those cities¦108276 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108277.
\s1 The allocation to Asher's descendants
\rem /s1 The Territory of Asher; Allotment for Asher; The Land Given to Asher; The Territory Assigned to Asher
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 24 The fifth¦108282 draw went¦108280 to Asher's¦108286 descendants¦108284 according¦108287 to their¦108287 clans¦108287.
\v 25 \add ≈Their land\add* \add included the cities of\add* Helkat¦108291, Hali¦108292, Beten¦108293, Akshaf,
\v 26 Allammelek¦108296, Amad, and Mishal¦108298. Their \add western\add* \add @border\add* started at¦108300 Mt. Karmel¦108300 and Shihorlibnat¦108302
\v 27 and turned¦108305 back¦108305 to the east to Beyt-Dagon¦108309 and the border with¦108311 Zebulun¦108311 and the Yiftah-El valley¦108315 to the north. Then¦108305 it went¦108320 to Beyt-Emek and Neiel¦108319 and north to Kabul,
\v 28 Abdon, Rehob¦108327, Hammon¦108328 and¦108326 Kanah¦108329, as far as Greater Sidon¦108331.
\v 29 The border¦108344 then¦108334 turned back to Ramah¦108336 and to the fortified¦108340 city¦108339 of Tsor¦108342 \add (commonly known as Tyre)\add* and turns¦108343 \add ≈west\add* to Hosah¦108345 coming out at the \add @Mediterranean\add* near Akzib¦108351.
\v 30 \add It also included\add* Ummah¦108353, Afek¦108354, and¦108353 Rehob¦108355—\add a total of\add* twenty-two¦108357 cities¦108356 as well as their¦108359 \add surrounding\add* villages¦108359.
\v 31 That was¦108362 Asher's¦108366 descendants' inheritance¦108362 according to¦108367 their clans¦108367, \add including\add* those cities¦108368 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108370.
\s1 The allocation to Naftali's descendants
\rem /s1 Allotment for Naphtali; The Territory Assigned to Naphtali; The Territory of Naphtali; The Land Given to Naphtali
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 32 The¦108379 sixth¦108377 draw went¦108375 to Naftali's¦108374 descendants according to their¦108380 clans¦108380.
\v 33 Their¦108383 border¦108383 started in¦108386 Helef (where there was¦108382 an oak tree¦108385 at Zaanannim¦108386) then¦108382 Adami-Nekeb and Yabneel and on¦108386 to¦108390 Lakkum¦108392 before exiting at the¦108395 Yordan¦108395.
\v 34 Then¦108397 \add *it¦108397\add* turned¦108397 west to Aznot¦108400-Tabor¦108401 and from¦108403 there¦108403 to Hukkok¦108404, meeting \add the border\add* with Zebulun¦108406 on the south¦108407, \add the border\add* with Asher¦108408 on the west, and \add the border\add* with Yehudah¦108411 on the east.
\v 35 The fortified¦108417 cities¦108416 were Tsiddim, Tser, Hammat¦108420, Rakkat¦108421, Kinneret¦108422,
\v 36 Adamah, Ramah¦108425, Hatsor,
\v 37 Kedesh, Edrei¦108429, Eyn-Hatsor,
\v 38 Yiron¦108433, Migdal¦108434-El, Horem¦108437, Beyt-Anat, and¦108433 Beyt-Shemesh—\add a total of\add* nineteen cities¦108443 as well as their¦108447 \add surrounding\add* villages¦108447.
\v 39 That was¦108450 Naftali's¦108454 descendants' inheritance¦108450 according to¦108455 their clans¦108455, \add including\add* those cities¦108456 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108457.
\s1 The allocation to Dan's descendants
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Dan; Allotment for Dan; The Territory of Dan; The Territory Assigned to Dan
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 40 The \add final\add* seventh¦108467 draw went¦108465 to Dan's¦108463 descendants¦108461 according to their¦108464 clans¦108464.
\v 41 \add ≈Their land\add* \add included the cities of\add* Tsorah¦108472, Eshtaol¦108473, Ir-Shemesh¦108474,
\v 42 Shaalabbin¦108477, Ayyalon, and¦108477 Yitlah,
\v 43 Elon, Timnah¦108482, Ekron¦108483,
\v 44 Eltekeh¦108485, Gibbeton¦108486, Baalat¦108487,
\v 45 Yehud, Bene-Berak, Gat-Rimmon,
\v 46 Meyarkon, Rakkon¦108499, and¦108499 the area opposite¦108503 Yafo¦108504 \add !(Joppa¦108504)\add*.
\v 47 Dan's border¦108526 went¦108506 out¦108506 from¦108512 them.\f + \fr 19:47 \ft Translations vary widely here because we're not sure what is meant by the literal rendering that we've kept here.\f* Then¦108506 Dan's descendants¦108514 battled against Leshem and captured¦108521 it and \add ≈slaughtered their inhabitants\add*. \add ≈So¦108506\add* they took¦108529 it over and settled in¦108532 Leshem \add ≈but¦108506\add* they renamed it to ‘Dan’ after their ancestor¦108538.\x + \xo 19:47: \xt Jdg 18:27-29.\x*
\v 48 That was¦108541 Dan's¦108545 descendants' inheritance¦108541 according to¦108546 their clans¦108546, \add including\add* those cities¦108547 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108549.
\s1 Yehoshua's allocation
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Joshua; The Final Assignment of the Land; Allotment for Joshua; Joshua's Inheritance
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 49 \add ≈After the allocation of the blocks of land¦108557 to¦108564 the various tribes\add*, the \add ≈Israelis¦108562\add* gave¦108559 Yehoshua (Nun's¦108567 son¦108565) his \add own\add* inheritance¦108563 among¦108568 them¦108568.
\p
\v 50 \add ≈Following Yahweh's¦108573 instructions to¦108575 give¦108574 Yehoshua whatever\add* city he asked¦108580 for¦108580, he was given Timnat¦108583-Serah¦108585 in the¦108586 hill¦108586 country¦108586 of¦108586 Efrayim¦108587 and he built¦108588 \add up\add* that¦108579 city and lived¦108592 in it¦108593.
\p
\v 51 Those were the allotments that¦108597 Eleazar¦108599 the priest¦108600 and Yehoshua (Nun's¦108605 son¦108603) gave¦108598 to the \add ≈leaders\add* of the Israeli¦108611 tribes¦108608 as their inheritances¦108596. It was done by¦108613 throwing dice there in Shiloh¦108615 in front¦108616 of Yahweh¦108617 at¦108613 the opening of the sacred¦108619 tent¦108619, and so the land¦108625 division was completed.
\c 20
\s1 The refuge cities
\rem /s1 Cities of Refuge; Cities of refuge; The Cities of Refuge
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦108629 told Yehoshua,\x + \xo 20:1-9: \xt Num 35:9-34; Deu 4:41-43; 19:1-13.\x*
\v 2 “Tell the¦108638 Israelis¦108639 to select some cities¦108645 that¦108647 people¦108638 can flee to in¦108651 order to be safe, just as I instructed you through Mosheh¦108653,
\v 3 so that if \add ≈someone accidentally¦108661 kills someone else\add*, they¦108665 can escape there¦108656 and¦108665 be¦108665 safe \add ≈from¦108668 the dead person's¦108660 family\add*.
\v 4 When¦108671 \add @that person\add* flees¦108671 to one¦108674 of these¦108677 cities¦108676, \add they must\add* stand¦108678 at¦108683 the city gate¦108680 and tell the elders¦108684 there what happened. Then¦108671 they should bring \add @the person\add* into the city and give¦108696 \add ≈them a place¦108699 there to live in¦108683\add*.
\v 5 \add ≈Now\add* if a relative of the deceased comes to avenge¦108705 the death, \add @the city elders¦108710\add* won't¦108708 hand¦108714 over the killer¦108713 because \add ≈the death was accidental and¦108703 didn't¦108708 happen because of hate¦108725 or premeditation\add*.
\v 6 \add ≈So¦108731 then that person\add* must stay in the city until they're brought before \add ≈the panel of judges¦108740\add*. \add If they decide that the death wasn't deliberate,\add* the person must remain in that city until the death of the high priest¦108744, then they can \add freely\add* return¦108752 to their own city and¦108731 own home.”
\p
\v 7 \add ≈So¦108769\add* \add @the Israelis\add* chose Kedesh¦108772 (in the Galilee¦108773 region in the hill country of Naftali¦108775) and Shekem¦108778 (in the hill country of Efrayim¦108780) and Kiriat¦108783-Arba¦108784 (\add ≈now called\add* Hebron¦108786, in the hill country of Yehudah¦108788).
\v 8 On the other¦108790 side¦108790 of the Yordan¦108791 \add river\add*, they¦108794 chose Betser (in the wilderness¦108798 on¦108798 the plateau¦108799 from the tribe of Reuben¦108801), Ramot¦108804 (in the Gilead¦108805 from the tribe of Gad¦108808), and¦108790 Golan¦108811 (in the Bashan¦108813 from the tribe of Menashsheh¦108815).
\v 9 Those were¦108818 the appointed¦108820 cities¦108819 for \add ≈both Israelis¦108824 and foreigners living among¦108827\add* them¦108827, so that anyone¦108832 who¦108832 accidentally¦108835 killed someone could flee¦108828 there¦108829 and \add ≈be safe from being avenged¦108839 by¦108838 the deceased's relatives\add* until¦108841 \add ≈they¦108818 could receive a proper trial\add*.
\c 21
\s1 The allocation to Levi's descendants
\rem /s1 Towns for the Levites; The Cities of the Levites; Cities Allotted to the Levites; The Towns Given to the Levites
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then the \add ≈leaders\add* of the Levites¦108851 went to Eleazar¦108854 the priest¦108855 and to Yehoshua (Nun's¦108861 son¦108859) and to the \add ≈Israeli¦108868 elders\add*\x + \xo 21:2: \xt Num 35:1-8.\x*
\v 2 at¦108878 Shiloh¦108872 (in the¦108878 Canaan¦108874 region¦108873) and¦108870 told¦108877 them, “Yahweh¦108876 said¦108870 \add ≈through\add* Mosheh¦108880 \add ≈that we should be given¦108881 cities¦108884 to live¦108885 in, along with¦108878 their¦108886 surrounding fields\add* for¦108887 our¦108887 livestock¦108887.”
\v 3 \add ≈So¦108889 the Israeli¦108892\add* \add leaders\add* gave¦108889 these¦108902 cities¦108901 and¦108889 the fields around them to the Levites¦108893 for their¦108905 inheritance¦108894 \add ≈as Yahweh¦108898 had instructed\add*:
\p
