\c 22
\s1 The eastern tribes return home
\rem /s1 The Eastern Tribes Return to Their Territory; Eastern Tribes Return Home; Joshua Sends the Eastern Tribes Home; The Eastern Tribes Return Home
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then¦109649 Yehoshua \add ≈summoned¦109650\add* the tribes¦109655 of Reuben and Gad, and the Menashsheh¦109656 half-tribe
\v 2 and¦109671 told them¦109659, “You yourselves have¦109661 obeyed¦109671 everything that Yahweh's¦109670 servant¦109669 Mosheh¦109668 instructed¦109666 you to do. In addition¦109658, you've all¦109673 followed everything that I told you.\x + \xo 22:2: \xt Num 32:20-32; Josh 1:12-15.\x*
\v 3 You've all \add ^supported\add* your \add ≈fellow tribes\add* all this time¦109686 and¦109691 fulfilled what your god¦109697 Yahweh¦109696 \add ≈requested of you¦109681 all\add*,
\v 4 and¦109699 now \add *he\add* has¦109700 enabled \add ≈these other tribes\add* to rest¦109700 \add from battle\add* just¦109704 like he told them¦109706 he would. \add ≈So¦109699\add* now, you all may go¦109709 back to your¦109715 homes that¦109716 Yahweh's¦109701 servant¦109721 Mosheh¦109720 gave¦109718 you on¦109723 the \add ≈other\add* side¦109723 of¦109723 the river.
\v 5 Only do¦109730 take¦109728 care¦109728 to \add continue to\add* obey the instructions and the law¦109736 that¦109737 Yahweh's¦109743 servant¦109741 Mosheh¦109740 gave you: to love¦109744 your god¦109748 Yahweh, to \add ≈follow him and his instructions\add*, to \add ≈stay close to him\add*, and to serve¦109758 him with all¦109759 your hearts¦109761 and your \add inner\add* selves.”
\v 6 Then¦109766 Yehoshua¦109767 blessed¦109766 them and¦109766 sent¦109768 them on their way to return to their \add ≈homes\add*.
\v 7 (Mosheh¦109780 had given the Bashan¦109781 to the half of the Menashsheh¦109778 half-tribe, and¦109782 Yehoshua had given \add land\add* on¦109781 the \add ≈western\add* side¦109788 of the Yordan¦109791 to the other¦109788 half.) \add When\add* he'd blessed¦109800 them¦109800
\v 8 he'd said¦109802, “Go back to your \add ≈homes\add* with many riches¦109805: plenty of livestock¦109811, and with silver¦109815, gold¦109816, bronze¦109817, and iron¦109818, and with lots of clothing¦109819. Share the plunder from your enemies¦109825 with \add ≈those who remained behind\add*.”
\v 9 So \add ≈the warriors from the tribes¦109841 of\add* Reuven, Gad¦109838, and the Menashsheh¦109842 half-tribe left the \add ≈others\add* there at¦109863 Shiloh¦109846 in the Canaan¦109850 region¦109848, and went¦109832 back to¦109856 their¦109859 own¦109859 land¦109858 in Gilead¦109855 \add across the river\add* which they¦109861 had¦109861 taken for themselves with¦109863 the agreement of Yahweh¦109867 given through Mosheh¦109870.
\s1 The altar by the Yordan
\rem /s1 A Memorial Altar East of the Jordan; The Altar by the Jordan; The Eastern Tribes Build a Memorial
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 10 \add ≈The warriors from the tribes¦109888 of\add* Reuven, Gad¦109886, and the Menashsheh¦109889 half-tribe arrived at the Yordan¦109894 river (still on the Canaan¦109879 side) and they¦109872 built¦109880 a very large¦109896 and noticeable altar there¦109890 \add before crossing over to go home\add*.
\v 11 \add When\add* the \add other\add* \add ≈Israelis¦109902\add* heard¦109899 \add about it\add*, they¦109905 said¦109903, “Look, the men \add ≈from the tribes¦109913 of\add* Reuven, Gad¦109911, and¦109899 the Menashsheh¦109914 half-tribe have¦109905 built¦109905 the altar¦109917 at the \add ≈entrance to this\add* Canaan¦109922 region¦109921 down at the Yordan¦109926 on \add *our\add* side¦109929.”
\p
\v 12 \add ≈Hearing that, those from the western side of the Yordan assembled¦109936 at Shiloh¦109943 to go¦109944 to battle¦109946 with the two and¦109936 a half tribes on¦109945 the eastern side\add*.
\v 13 \add Meanwhile\add*, they¦109949 sent¦109949 the priest¦109979 Finehas (Eleazar's¦109978 son¦109976) \add across\add* into the Gilead¦109972 region¦109971 \add to talk\add* with \add the leaders from\add* the tribes¦109966 of Reuben¦109957, Gad¦109962, and the Menashsheh¦109968 half-tribe.
\v 14 \add @Finehas\add* took ten¦109981 leaders with¦109983 him—important leaders from each of the Israeli¦109991 tribes¦109991 \add from the western side\add*.
\v 15 They \add crossed over\add* to the Gilead¦110022 region¦110021 to talk to \add the leaders from\add* the tribes¦110016 of Reuben¦110007, Gad¦110012, and¦110002 the Menashsheh¦110018 half-tribe. They said¦110023,
\v 16 “Yahweh's¦110032 people are \add ≈asking\add*, ‘What's¦110033 this¦110036 unfaithfulness¦110035 that¦110037 you all¦110029 have¦110038 done unfaithfully¦110038 against Yisrael's¦110040 god¦110039—turning¦110041 away from¦110043 Yahweh when¦110045 you built¦110045 an altar¦110047 for yourselves¦110045 today in¦110039 rebellion¦110048 against Yahweh?\x + \xo 22:16: \xt Deu 12:13-14.\x*
\v 17 Wasn't \add ≈our disobedience at¦110069 Peor¦110058\add*\x + \xo 22:17: \xt Num 25:1-9.\x* \add ≈bad enough¦110052 for¦110054 you\add*? We¦110062 haven't \add ≈gotten over it¦110063\add* to¦110054 this¦110066 day¦110065. Plus there was¦110067 a \add ≈deadly disease\add* among¦110069 Yahweh's¦110070 people.
\v 18 But¦110072 all of you—are you turning¦110073 away from Yahweh today? If you all rebel¦110079 against¦110083 Yahweh today, tomorrow¦110082 he'll be furious at¦110081 all of us.
\v 19 But¦110091 if¦110092 it's because you all think this land here is defiled, then¦110091 cross¦110097 back over¦110097 to¦110098 Yahweh's own¦110096 land where¦110104 he lives in¦110111 his sacred¦110108 tent¦110108. \add ≈Either way\add* don't¦110113 rebel against¦110112 Yahweh by building¦110120 \add this other\add* altar for yourselves that's distinct from¦110123 our¦110111 god¦110126 Yahweh's altar.
\v 20 Didn't Akan act¦110134 unfaithfully¦110134 \add ≈taking something that was forbidden\add*\x + \xo 22:20: \xt Josh 7:1-26.\x* and¦110137 \add ≈all¦110139 of us suffered as a result of it¦110143\add*? \add ≈It¦110143 wasn't just him alone that died¦110149 because of that\add*.’ ”
\p
\v 21 \add The leaders from\add* the tribes¦110161 of Reuben¦110156, Gad¦110159, and the Menashsheh¦110162 half-tribe answered¦110153 \add ≈the other leaders\add*,
\v 22 “Yahweh is the god of gods. Yahweh is the god of gods. He¦110180 knows, and¦110182 as for \add ≈the Israeli people\add*, let¦110184 \add #them\add* know¦110184 \add also\add*—if it¦110184 was in rebellion¦110187 or in unfaithfulness¦110190 against Yahweh, don't¦110192 \add ≈bother trying to save¦110194 us¦110194 today\add*.
\v 23 If \add ≈we'd aimed\add* to build¦110198 an altar¦110200 for ourselves to turn¦110201 \add away\add* from¦110202 following¦110202 Yahweh, or if it was to offer¦110206 burnt¦110208 offerings or grain¦110209 offerings on it, or if to make the sacrifices¦110214 of¦110214 peace¦110215 offerings on it, Yahweh himself will \add ≈handle it\add*.
\v 24 \add ≈But¦110220 no, we did it because¦110224 we foresaw a potential problem: what if in the future, your descendants ask our¦110233 descendants\add* \add over here on this side of the river\add*, ‘What¦110235 \add ≈do you¦110237 lot have¦110225 to do with\add* Yisrael's¦110240 god¦110239 Yahweh¦110238?
\v 25 \add ≈Yahweh has¦110243 given this Yordan¦110256 river as a border¦110242 between¦110246 us¦110246, and you descendants of¦110248 Reuben¦110250 and Gad¦110253\add*. \add ≈You all don't¦110257 have any part\add* in¦110261 Yahweh.’ Then¦110242 your descendants might make our¦110266 descendants \add ≈stop worshipping\add* Yahweh.
\v 26 \add ≈So¦110279 we¦110273 decided\add* to build¦110278 the¦110281 altar¦110281—not to be used for burnt¦110283 offerings¦110283 or for sacrifices¦110285,
\v 27 but¦110291 as a \add ≈symbol to remind\add* our future descendants and yours, that \add ≈we all truly worship Yahweh\add* with¦110301 our burnt¦110301 offerings, our sacrifices¦110302, and our peace¦110303 offerings, so your¦110307 descendants can't¦110304 tell our future descendants that \add ≈we have no business worshipping\add* Yahweh.
\v 28 \add ≈If¦110318 they¦110320 do say¦110320 anything like that, then¦110316 our descendants¦110324 will¦110326 be able to reply\add*, ‘See that copy¦110330 of Yahweh's¦110332 altar¦110331 which¦110333 isn't¦110337 used for burnt¦110338 offerings¦110338 or sacrifices¦110340, our ancestors¦110336 built that as a reminder for both you all and¦110316 us¦110345.’
\v 29 May any idea of rebelling¦110351 against¦110352 Yahweh stay far from us. \add ≈Same with¦110352 any idea of\add* building¦110357 any altar apart from our¦110365 god¦110365 Yahweh's¦110352 \add genuine\add* altar for¦110359 burnt¦110359 offerings, or grain¦110360 offerings, or other¦110362 sacrifices¦110361.”
\p
\v 30 \add ≈So\add* Finehas the priest¦110373 and the other community and clan leaders¦110374 with¦110395 him¦110380, listened¦110371 to what the descendants¦110386 of Reuven, Gad¦110391, and Menashsheh¦110393 told them, and it¦110394 \add ≈sounded sensible to them\add*,
\v 31 \add ≈so\add* Finehas (\add the late\add* Eleazar's¦110401 son¦110399) told \add *them\add*, “Today we¦110419 realise that Yahweh is¦110422 among¦110422 us and¦110397 that you all haven't acted¦110427 unfaithfully¦110427 against¦110428 \add *him\add*, so therefore you've prevented Yahweh \add ≈from¦110437 needing to punish us\add*.”
\p
\v 32 Then¦110440 Finehas and the other leaders¦110447 left Gilead¦110457 and returned¦110440 back \add across the Yordan\add* to¦110458 the Canaan¦110461 region¦110456 where \add ≈most of¦110460 the Israelis¦110465 resided\add*, taking back a \add good\add* report.
\v 33 \add ≈The people¦110473 were pleased with that¦110488 news¦110471\add*, and they¦110475 \add ≈thanked\add* God¦110476 and stopped talking about going¦110481 to war¦110483 with Reuven and Gad¦110494 \add across the river\add* and destroying¦110484 \add *them\add*.
\p
\v 34 The¦110499 descendants¦110499 of Reuven and¦110502 Gad¦110504 named the¦110502 altar¦110505 \add ‘Reminder’\add* because¦110506 it¦110508 was a reminder between¦110509 them that Yahweh¦110511 is God¦110512.
\c 23
\s1 Yehoshua's final speech
\rem /s1 Joshua's Farewell to the Leaders; Joshua Exhorts the People; Joshua's farewell and death; Joshua's Final Words to Israel; Joshua's Farewell Address
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 \add ≈A long time¦110516 passed\add* and Yahweh¦110522 had¦110521 given¦110521 Yisrael¦110523 \add ≈peace without attacks\add* from¦110524 their¦110526 enemies¦110526 all¦110524 around, and Yehoshua was¦110529 \add now\add* \add ≈in¦110531 his old¦110529 age\add*,
\v 2 \add ≈so\add* he¦110533 summoned all¦110535 the Israeli elders¦110538 and leaders, along with the judges¦110540 and officials¦110541. He¦110542 told them¦110543, “Now I'm in¦110547 my old¦110545 age,
\v 3 \add ≈but¦110549\add* you all have¦110550 seen¦110550 what Yahweh¦110556 did¦110555 to¦110558 all those \add ≈kingdoms¦110560\add* ahead of you, because¦110562 \add *he's¦110566\add* the¦110567 one¦110567 who¦110567 fights¦110567 for¦110568 you all.
\v 4 I've¦110571 allocated the remaining¦110576 \add ≈kingdoms¦110575\add* that you¦110572 all¦110583 will defeat as an¦110578 inheritance¦110578 for¦110579 your¦110579 tribes¦110579, alongside those that I conquered from¦110580 the Yordan¦110582 to the Mediterranean in¦110578 the west
\v 5 Your¦110597 god¦110594 Yahweh¦110607 will¦110596 push them¦110596 out¦110596 ahead of you all and¦110593 capture their¦110604 lands for you to possess¦110601, just¦110605 as¦110605 \add *he\add* told you he would.
\v 6 Take¦110615 great care to obey and¦110611 do¦110614 everything¦110616 that Mosheh¦110621 wrote¦110618 down—don't¦110622 deviate from¦110625 it¦110625 in¦110619 any way.
\v 7 Don't¦110629 enter those remaining¦110634 \add ≈kingdoms¦110632\add*, and don't mention the¦110637 name¦110637 of their gods¦110638 or make an oath using their names¦110637 and don't worship¦110647 or bow¦110647 down¦110647 to¦110648 them¦110648.
\v 8 Instead you all should cling¦110655 to¦110653 your god¦110654 Yahweh¦110653, just¦110656 as¦110656 you've done¦110657 until¦110658 now.
\v 9 \add Yes,\add* Yahweh¦110663 has driven¦110662 away many great¦110666 kingdoms¦110665 ahead of you all, and¦110662 until¦110674 this day¦110675, none of them have stood¦110671 against you.
\v 10 Just one of you \add ≈can make a thousand¦110684 men flee\add*, because¦110685 Yahweh¦110687 is your¦110681 god¦110688—he's the¦110690 one who¦110690 fights¦110690 for¦110691 you just¦110692 \add ≈like he said he would\add*.\x + \xo 23:10: a \xt Deu 32:30; \xo b \xt Deu 3:22.\x*
\v 11 \add ≈Make¦110700 a great effort to guard yourselves\add* that you all \add continue\add* to love¦110699 your god¦110703 Yahweh¦110702.
\v 12 \add Yes,\add* if you all ever¦110709 turn away \add from him\add* and instead cling¦110711 to¦110712 those remaining kingdoms¦110713 or remaining people, and if you intermarry¦110718 with them or associate¦110720 with them,
\v 13 you all will certainly \add soon\add* find out that your god Yahweh will not continue to¦110732 drive¦110732 out these¦110736 nations¦110735 \add ≈ahead of¦110737 you\add*. Then they¦110738 will \add end up\add* trapping and snaring you all, and be like a whip on your sides¦110743 and like thorns¦110744 in¦110743 your eyes¦110745, until¦110746 you all perish¦110748 from¦110749 on this¦110752 good¦110751 land that Yahweh your god has¦110754 given¦110754 you.
\p
\v 14 Listen, today I'm about to go the way¦110763 \add ≈that everyone¦110779 has to go\add* and you all know¦110767 with all your heart¦110770 and with all your soul that not¦110775 one thing has \add ≈failed to come¦110790 true\add* from¦110780 all the good¦110783 things¦110782 that your god¦110787 Yahweh¦110786 said about you. \add ≈Everything¦110789 has happened as said—down to the very last word\add*.
\v 15 And \add ≈just¦110800 like all those good things came¦110802 true\add*, so¦110813 \add too\add* Yahweh¦110810 will¦110814 \add ≈send all the punishments he promised you all\add* \add if you disobey him\add*, \add ≈even if it means that\add* he destroys¦110824 you all from¦110826 this good land that \add *he's¦110831\add* given¦110831 you.
\v 16 If¦110854 you ignore the agreement¦110839 with¦110855 your god¦110841 Yahweh¦110840 and \add disobey\add* his commands¦110843 and go¦110845 and serve¦110846 other¦110848 gods¦110847 and bow¦110849 down¦110849 to¦110850 them¦110850, then \add *his\add* \add ≈anger¦110852 will¦110851 flare up\add* against you all and you'll quickly¦110857 \add ≈be wiped out\add* from¦110858 the good¦110860 land¦110859 that¦110842 he¦110862 has¦110862 given¦110862 you.”
\c 24
\s1 The promise again of Yisrael's descendants
\rem /s1 The Covenant Renewed at Shechem; The Lord's Covenant Renewed; Joshua Speaks to the People at Shechem; The Tribes Renew the Covenant
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then Yehoshua assembled all¦110870 the¦110872 tribes¦110872 of¦110872 Yisrael¦110873 at Shekem¦110874. He¦110875 summoned their elders¦110876, leaders, judges¦110879, and officers¦110880, and they¦110881 presented¦110881 themselves¦110881 before¦110882 God¦110883,
\v 2 and Yehoshua told all¦110889 the people¦110891, “Yahweh¦110895, the god¦110896 of Yisrael¦110897 says¦110894: Your ancestors¦110901 \add including\add* Terah¦110903 the father of Abraham¦110905 and Nahor¦110907, lived beyond¦110898 the \add Euphrates\add* river¦110899 from¦110902 long¦110902 ago¦110902, \add ≈but¦110885\add* they¦110908 \add ≈worshipped\add* other¦110910 gods¦110909.\x + \xo 24:2: \xt Gen 11:27.\x*
\v 3 Then¦110912 I took¦110912 your ancestor¦110915 Abraham¦110918 from¦110919 beyond¦110919 the river¦110920 and brought him \add ≈across\add* all¦110923 the land¦110925 of¦110925 Canaan¦110926, and I multiplied¦110927 his¦110931 \add ≈descendants\add*, \add ≈including¦110921\add* giving¦110932 him Isaac¦110937.\x + \xo 24:3: a \xt Gen 12:1-9; \xo b \xt Gen 21:1-3.\x*
